al screening to final interview.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You put Cosuno on the map in the Berlin and European tech community, through referrals, meetups and content with our engineers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You advise on levelling, compensation and market trends, so our offers win.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You make hiring measurable with a monthly dashboard on time-to-hire, conversion and source of hire.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What the job really looks like</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The best engineers rarely apply. Most of your hires come from your own outreach, so a large part of your week is sourcing and candidate conversations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You compete with big tech and AI companies for the same people, and you need a compelling story to win them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You talk shop with engineers. You do not need to code, but you understand what a TypeScript full-stack role or an ML engineering role really involves.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">There is no large TA team and no finished playbook. You build the processes while you hire.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You push back when a profile, a process or a decision is not right. We want you to.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What you bring</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At least 4 years of recruiting experience, of which at least 2 years in-house at a high-growth tech company, hiring software engineers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record you can prove in numbers: hires made, time-to-hire and offer acceptance rate. You steer your pipeline by data, not gut feeling.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technical fluency: you understand modern tech stacks and roles (full-stack, backend, AI/ML, platform) well enough to assess candidates and challenge hiring managers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven technical sourcing skills across LinkedIn, GitHub and tech communities, including Boolean and X-ray searches.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Structured assessment: you have built interview loops with engineering teams and keep them fair, fast and consistent.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong closing skills: you win engineers against competing offers, including from big tech and AI companies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent English, written and spoken.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Nice to have</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">German language skills.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience hiring AI/ML engineers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with cross-border hiring in Europe, including Employer of Record set-ups.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with Ashby, LinkedIn Recruiter, Clay or Lusha.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curiosity about construction or other traditional industries.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What we offer</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Salary:</strong> €70,000–90,000 gross base salary per year, depending on experience, plus a variable component of 25 % of your base salary at 100 % target achievement, tied to hires who successfully complete their probation period.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI at the core:</strong> you work with Ashby, LinkedIn Recruiter and you have a budget to test new tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learning budget</strong> for your professional development.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Time off:</strong> 25 vacation days per year, rising by one day for each year with Cosuno up to a maximum of 28 days. On top of that, 24 and 31 December are always off.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Flexibility:</strong> fully remote within Germany or from our 