ea is at the heart of it. As a Working Student, you will be the bridge between our engineering teams and the lab. Engineers bring you the parts they need; you turn their requests into a clear plan, pick the right printer and material, and deliver a finished part on time.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">Because many teams need prints at once, you will balance competing requests, keep everyone updated on status and make sure our fleet of around 30 printers runs reliably every day.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3>Your roadmap to make an impact</h3><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Print requests:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> Take requests from engineering, clarify material, tolerances, quantity and deadline, and give honest feedback on printability</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Print preparation:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> Prepare and slice models for FDM and resin printers, choosing settings, orientation and supports for each part</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Capacity planning:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> Plan and track capacity across around 30 printers, prioritise competing requests and keep requesters updated on status</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Maintenance:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> Carry out routine and preventive maintenance, including nozzle and hot end changes, calibration, cleaning, belt and bed checks, firmware updates and resin tank care</span></p></li></ul><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Supplier repairs:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> Organise service jobs with suppliers for repairs beyond in-house maintenance and follow them up until each printer is back in operation</span></p></li></ul><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Lab organisation:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> Keep the 3D Printing Area clean, safe and organised, including filament and resin stock, spare parts and consumables</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Continuous improvement:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> Make the area work better through improved workflows, storage, labelling, documentation and request tracking</span></p></li></ul> <br> <ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Currently enrolled at a university, ideally in mechanical engineering, mechatronics, product design, aerospace or a related field</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">A real passion for 3D printing: you print in your free time, tinker with your own machines or follow the community</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Hands-on experience with FDM printers, ideally Prusa (CORE ONE L) and Bambu Lab (X1 Carbon, X1E, H2D, H2S, AMS)</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Confident with slicers such as PrusaSlicer, Bambu Studio or OrcaSlicer</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Very organised: you can plan, prioritise and track many requests at once without losing the overview</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Clear communicator in English. German is a plus</span></p></li></ul><h4><span style="color:#000000">Nice to have</span></h4><ul><li><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">Experience with Formlabs resin printers and PreForm, including post-processing (washing, curing).</span></p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">Basic CAD skills to make small fixes to models before printing.</span></p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">Knowledge of engineering materials (PLA, PETG, ASA, PA-CF and similar) and when to use them.</span></p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">Experience with print farm or queue management tools.</span></p></li></ul><h3><strong><span style="color:#121317">Why TYTAN?</span></strong></h3><ul><li><p><strong><span style="