&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Deliveroo is now part of DoorDash, bringing together teams with even greater reach, scale, and ambition. Depending on your role, you may collaborate with teammates, systems, and leaders across DoorDash and Wolt. Together, we’re unlocking new possibilities as one global team.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an Engineering Manager to lead Codeless, our internal Server-Driven UI (SDUI) platform team. In this role, you will lead a cross-functional team bridging mobile/web frontend engineering and core platform backend systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While this role is deeply rooted in modern UI architecture, its mission goes beyond standard UI development: Codeless empowers product teams across the organization to ship dynamic, native UI experiences dynamically from the backend—eliminating app store release bottlenecks, dramatically accelerating feature iteration, and establishing a unified UI schema across iOS, Android, and Web.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll be doing&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a role with broad impact, from hands-on technical guidance to championing web and mobile accessibility across the company. We&#39;re looking for a leader who excels at fostering collaboration and can confidently guide a concept from initial idea to robust implementation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Day-to-day in this role you’ll:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership &amp;amp; Strategy: &lt;/strong&gt;Build, mentor, and scale an engineering team responsible for our core Server-Driven UI platform (&quot;Codeless&quot;). Foster an inclusive, high-ownership engineering culture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Platform Architecture &amp;amp; Evolution:&lt;/strong&gt; Oversee the design and evolution of dynamic layout engines, declarative UI schemas, and client rendering frameworks across iOS, Android, and Web.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Developer Velocity &amp;amp; Platform Adoption:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with product feature teams to drive internal adoption of Codeless. Ensure the platform provides exceptional Developer Experience, clear tooling, robust design system integration, and seamless debugging workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Execution &amp;amp; Quality:&lt;/strong&gt; Set high technical standards for platform performance, payload optimization, caching strategies, backward compatibility, and graceful offline/fallback behavior across client devices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Work closely with Product Managers, Design System leaders, and Core Infrastructure engineers to align the Codeless roadmap with broader company initiatives and global design paradigms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll need to thrive&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engineering Management:&lt;/strong&gt; 3+ years of experience managing software engineering teams, with a track record of coaching engineers, delivering complex platform initiatives, and driving technical strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;UI &amp;amp; Platform Domain Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong foundational background in mobile (iOS/Android) or modern web architecture (React, SwiftUI, Jetpack Compose, or declarative UI paradigms).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product &amp;amp; Platform Mindset:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Ability to treat internal product engineering teams as customers, evaluating platform success through developer velocity, adoption metrics, and rendering performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why join us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Deliveroo, you’ll do work that matters—solving real-world problems in a three-sided marketplace that’s constantly evolving. We’re food lovers, problem solvers, community builders and more, brought together by a shared drive to make things better. Working here you can expect to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🔧 Solve meaningful problems at real scale Work on a complex, always-on marketplace that impacts millions every day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌱 See your impact, fast Ship, test and improve ideas quickly in a low-hierarchy, high-ownership environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🧠 Grow through challenge and ownership Take on big, ambiguous problems and accelerate your career with strong support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌎 A culture built for builders High standards, collaboration, flexible working and continuous learning.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💰 Share in the success you help create Competitive salary and equity options, so you’re rewarded for the impact you make.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;➡️ Want a deeper look at how we build? Check out our Tech Blog.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We aim to create a fair process that lets your skills shine—our interview typically includes 3-4 stages. Explore our Engineering Interview Guide here to help you feel confident at each stage.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Diversity, Equity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;At Deliveroo, we know that a great workplace reflects the world around us and that true diversity and inclusion make us stronger, more creative, and better at what we do. We’re committed to fostering an environment where everyone can do their best work and feel they belong.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in equality of opportunity and welcome candidates from all backgrounds regardless of age, gender, ethnicity, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, socio-economic background, religion, or belief.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you have a disability or long-term health condition and need support to apply for one of our roles, or require any reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process, you’ll have the opportunity to let us know once you’ve submitted your application. We’ll share details on how to request support so we can ensure you have a fair and equitable experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re excited about making a real impact in a fast-moving marketplace and growing your career alongside ambitious, supportive teams, we’d love to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;Beware of recruitment scams: DASH Brands will never ask you to pay money or share sensitive financial information during hiring — learn more about DASH Brands&#39; legitimate recruiting process at&lt;/em&gt; &lt;a class=&quot;_ymio1r31 _ypr0glyw _zcxs1o36 _mizu194a _1ah3dkaa _ra3xnqa1 _128mdkaa _1cvmnqa1 _4davt94y _4bfu18uv _1hms8stv _ajmmnqa1 _vchhusvi _kqswh2mm _2rkolb4i _ect4ttxp _syaz13af _1a3b18uv _4fpr8stv _5goinqa1 _f8pj13af _9oik18uv _1bnxglyw _jf4cnqa1 _30l313af _1nrm18uv _c2waglyw _1iohnqa1 _9h8h12zz _10531ra0 _1ien1ra0 _n0fx1ra0 _1vhv17z1&quot; href=&quot;http://careersatdoordash.com/recruitment-scam-awareness&quot; data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot; data-is-router-link=&quot;false&quot; data-testid=&quot;link-with-safety&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;careersatdoordash.com/recruitment-scam-awareness&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/deliveroo/engineering-manager-server-driven-ui-codeless-london-141498","tags":["Engineering (Infra)"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1793127328},{"slug":"senior-electrical-product-engineer-maritime-engineering-sydney-australia-430192","company_name":"Andurilindustries","title":"Senior Electrical Product Engineer - Maritime Engineering","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Product Engineer is the primary electrical design engineering presence on the production floor, bridging the gap between design intent and production execution. The role sits within Platform Engineering and is based primarily at the production site, dispositioning nonconformances and Material Review Board (MRB) actions for electrical systems and sub-assemblies, resolving design questions in real time, and closing the loop between production and design so that issues get root caused and fixed at the source. To hold that authority credibly, this role also contributes to upstream electrical design - architecture, analysis, schematics, and design reviews - so they have the depth needed to make sound disposition decisions on the floor. This is a senior individual contributor role requiring strong technical judgement in electrical and power systems engineering, the ability to operate autonomously in a fast-paced production environment, and the credibility to influence both design engineers and production teams. You will be expected to drive systemic improvements, cutting repeat nonconformances through changes to the design and documentation, as well as resolving individual issues.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Production Floor Engineering Support&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary electrical design engineering point of contact on the production floor for assigned programs and product lines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the design authority at Material Review Board (MRB) for electrical systems, working with Quality and Manufacturing to minimise production hold time without compromising product safety and integrity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resolve production process-blockers, design ambiguities, and schematic/drawing interpretation issues in real time, exercising engineering judgement within defined authority boundaries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide rapid-response engineering support and Root Cause Analysis (RCA) to Production, Quality, and Test teams for electrical nonconformance resolution, use-as-is/rework/scrap decisions, and repair dispositions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and escalate systemic electrical design issues to core Design Engineering teams with clear problem statements, data, and recommended corrective actions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform detailed electrical calculations, simulations, and analysis to support MRB dispositions, deviation requests, and use-as-is justifications (e.g. power budgets, thermal derating, circuit analysis, connector/harness assessments)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Electrical Design Contribution&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the design, development and integration of electrical systems and subsystems, maintaining the technical depth needed to hold disposition authority on the production floor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform detailed electrical calculations, simulations and analysis (circuit analysis, power budgets, thermal derating, EMC/EMI) to support both design decisions and MRB dispositions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in design reviews (SRR, PDR, CDR) and contribute to system-level trade studies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally with mechanical, software, and systems engineering to integrate electrical systems into the vehicle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Design Intent Translation &amp;amp; Multi-Site Support&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the translation of electrical design intent into production-executable work across multiple product versions, configurations, and manufacturing sites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the stand-up and ramp of production at new or expanding manufacturing sites, ensuring electrical design engineering knowledge transfers effectively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise and implement engineering changes to correct production issues that originate in the electrical design, through the Anduril configuration management and change process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feed production observations, failure modes and DFM/DFA opportunities back into Platform Electrical design work through structured feedback, prioritised using data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Design to Production Interface&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Manufacturing Engineering on work instruction (WI) development, tooling validation, and First Article Inspection (FAI) activities for electrical assemblies, communicating the design intent and acceptance criteria&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the resolution of EBOM discrepancies found in production for electrical assemblies, and give engineering input to Configuration Management and Manufacturing Engineering on PLM workflows, BOM reconciliation and work instruction tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify patterns across electrical nonconformances, test failures and build issues, and lead engineering root cause analysis and design corrective action implementation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate on the improvement of key tool and functional interfaces (PLM workflows, digital work instructions, BOM reconciliation) that impact design-to-production efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the development of scalable frameworks for multi-site production: configuration management alignment, site-specific work instruction adaptation, and cross-site lesson-learned sharing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build repeatable playbooks for standing up production of new product variants, reducing ramp time and first-unit defects at each additional site&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration &amp;amp; Metrics&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain strong working relationships with Quality, Supply Chain, Manufacturing Engineering, and Program Management to ensure aligned priorities and rapid issue resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collate and drive corrective actions on design-originated production issues, providing data-backed prioritisation to core Design Engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in Production readiness reviews, design reviews (P&amp;amp;DFMEA, DFM/A/T) and engineering change assessments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key Competencies &amp;amp; Attributes&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engineering Judgement:&lt;/strong&gt; Technical depth in electrical and power systems combined with production pragmatism - able to make sound engineering decisions under time pressure without over-engineering solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design Authority Integrity:&lt;/strong&gt; You protect product safety and integrity under schedule pressure, understand the limits of your delegated authority and escalate when you should&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Influence:&lt;/strong&gt; Credibility with both design engineers and production operators; able to speak both languages and bridge communication gaps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Autonomy &amp;amp; Initiative:&lt;/strong&gt; Comfort with ambiguity and competing priorities in a fast-moving production environment; able to self-direct and prioritise without constant direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems Thinking:&lt;/strong&gt; Thinks beyond individual issue resolution to identify patterns, root causes, and scalable solutions that prevent recurrence across sites and variants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Clear, concise technical communication - written dispositions, engineering reports, and presentations to leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s or Master&#39;s degree in Electrical Engineering or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in a senior role within defence, tech or any fast-paced environment, driving successful electrical engineering projects from concept to market launch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in electrical engineering principles, techniques, and technologies, with a track record of delivering innovative solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in using industry-standard electrical design and simulation software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent interpersonal skills, with the ability to motivate and mentor junior engineers while fostering a culture of collaboration and innovation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong time management and organisational abilities, with a demonstrated ability to deliver projects on time and within budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent problem-solving skills, with the ability to think creatively and adapt to diverse and evolving challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to effectively communicate complex technical concepts to both technical and non-technical stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with fast paced environment best practices, including agility, adaptability, and the ability to work in a fast-paced and dynamic environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to obtain and maintain a NV2 Australian Government Security Clearance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated hands-on experience working on or directly supporting a production floor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of Material Review Board (MRB) processes, nonconformance management, and engineering disposition (use-as-is, rework, scrap, return to vendor)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing electrical and power systems for unmanned vehicles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the subsea or maritime domain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on defence programs and familiarity with current Defence standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience as a Product, Sustaining, Liaison or Production Support Engineer with delegated design or disposition authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with first article inspection (e.g. AS9102) and production test development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with IPC/WHMA-A-620 and/or IPC-A-610&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The salary range for this role is an estimate based on a wide range of compensation factors, inclusive of base salary only. Actual salary offer may vary based on (but not limited to) work experience, education and/or training, critical skills, and/or business considerations. Highly competitive equity grants are included in the majority of full time offers; and are considered part of Anduril&#39;s total compensation package. Additionally, Anduril offers top-tier benefits for full-time employees, including:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;At Anduril, we invest in our people. Our comprehensive, competitive benefits package (available at little to no cost to employees) ensures you’re supported in health, recovery, and whatever comes next.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;For more information, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.anduril.com/careers&quot;&gt;Explore Our Benefits&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;RichText column1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Protecting Yourself from Recruitment Scams&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;Anduril is committed to maintaining the integrity of our Talent acquisition process and the security of our candidates. We&#39;ve observed a rise in sophisticated phishing and fraudulent schemes where individuals impersonate Anduril representatives, luring job seekers with false interviews or job offers. These scammers often attempt to extract payment or sensitive personal information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;RichText column2&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;To ensure your safety and help you navigate your job search with confidence, please keep the following critical points in mind:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No Financial Requests:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Anduril will never solicit payment or demand personal financial details (such as banking information, credit card numbers, or social security numbers) at any stage of our hiring process. Our legitimate recruitment is entirely free for candidates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please always verify communications:&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct from Anduril: If you receive an email from one of our recruiters, it will &lt;em&gt;only&lt;/em&gt; come from an ----- address.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Via Agency Partner: If contacted by a recruiting agency for an Anduril role, their email will clearly identify their agency. If you suspect any suspicious activity, please verify the agency&#39;s authenticity by reaching out to &lt;a ----------
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exercise Caution with Unsolicited Outreach:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;If you receive any communication that appears suspicious, contains grammatical errors, or makes unusual requests, do not engage. Always confirm the sender&#39;s email domain is ----- before providing any personal information or clicking on links.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What to Do If You Suspect Fraud:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Should you encounter any questionable or fraudulent outreach claiming to be from Anduril, please report it immediately to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a ---------- Your proactive caution is invaluable in protecting your personal information and upholding the security and trustworthiness of our recruitment efforts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Privacy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;To view Anduril&#39;s candidate data privacy policy, please visit &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Hyperlink&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/&quot;&gt;https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;By submitting your application, you consent to Anduril Industries using a third-party service provider to conduct pre-employment risk, integrity, and due diligence screening and assessing potential risks as part of your application process. This third-party service provider provides risk-intelligence services that may include analysis of sanctions and watchlists, adverse media, public-record information, and other lawful open-source or commercial data sources. This third-party service provider does not act as a consumer reporting agency. Use of this provider helps to ensure compliance with applicable laws and protect technology, intellectual property, and organizational security.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/andurilindustries/senior-electrical-product-engineer-maritime-engineering-sydney-australia-430192","tags":["Maritime & Maneuver Dominance : Undersea Dominance - Engineering & Operations : Software Engineering"],"job_types":[],"location":"Sydney, Australia","created_at":1793127327},{"slug":"manufacturing-test-engineer-sydney-australia-320593","company_name":"Andurilindustries","title":"Manufacturing Test Engineer","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;We are seeking a Manufacturing Test Engineer to join Anduril, working in a cutting-edge start-up environment to advance the state-of-the-possible in subsea robotics. The Manufacturing Test Engineer will be charged with developing and implementing high-fidelity, automated test processes on both the component and system level. Working closely with engineering staff and a team of skilled electro-mechanical technicians, this role is key to advancing our testing capabilities to ensure the highest levels quality are achieved as we continue drive scalability into our production operations.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Anduril’s Manufacturing team is producing the next generation of Autonomous Underwater Vehicles globally at rate. The Manufacturing Engineering team owns production readiness and process engineering across the Undersea Dominance product range — from core vehicle platform to specialised mission payloads, spanning mechanical and electrical hardware build through to full system integration &amp;amp; test.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You will own the test software, automation and tooling that proves every Dive-XL vehicle works before it leaves the building — the Python frameworks that drive instruments and vehicle hardware, the operator-facing GUIs that make complex test sequences safe and repeatable under production pressure, and the interlocks that protect people and product when the system is commanding real high-voltage DC. You will also own the infrastructure underneath: NixOS-based station builds, test result flow into MES, and the configuration management that keeps a fleet of test stations reproducible and rollback-safe. If you thrive hands-on — oscilloscopes and protocol analysers as often as a code editor — in a fast-paced environment where the architecture is yours to build, this role is for you.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a broad range of test capabilities across the manufacturing value stream - PCBA bring up, electrical boxes/bottles bring-up, system level checkouts and acceptance testing to key component level in process validation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, execute, and manage test eco-system to de-risk hardware and ensure product meets target reliability levels and ultimate design intent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform hands-on and data-driven root cause analysis of electromechanical subsystems utilizing structured problem solving methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, implement and maintain semi-automated testing equipment/protocols for subsystem characterization and testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diagnose production test issues hands-on as fist point of contact for test technicians. Isolate the failure mode, work with Electrical Design and Software when escalation is needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the design/systems team throughout product development cycles to perform risk assessments, maintain ownership of test deployment activities in production, oversee technician training, burn down bug fixes/improvements as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce and maintain testing logs/data, develop library of error codes with troubleshooting logic/diagrams for fast issue resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate controlled test instructions that can be easily followed by technician team in MES or other test execution systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize test design and execution of full system “end of line” factory acceptance test (FAT) of AUVs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and execution of PCBA and electrical system components with hands on testing and rework as necessary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;REQUIRED QUALIFIACTIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in Software, Computer, Electrical, Mechatronic or related field, or equivalent work experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in hardware testing and automated test systems (LabVIEW, Test Stand, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in programming languages such as Python, Matlab, SHELL, or others&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with computer hardware communication protocols: USB, Ethernet, RS232, RS485, PCIe, HDMI, CAN, etc&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in a relevant field, preferably test design of electro-mechanical hardware in a manufacturing environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are well versed with complex electromechanical systems and are passionate about understanding what it takes to make them work reliably&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience developing full system test plans and know how to execute them on fast-paced product development timelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience with programming/testing a wide range of sensors, actuators, and electrical components&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can prototype and run your own tests, from experimental setup to hardware and software implementation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to obtain and maintain an Australian Government NV2 Security Clearance (Australian citizen).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED QUALIFIACTIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in sub-sea robotics or AUV/UUV industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiar with Product Life Cycle (PLM) systems, Manufacturing Execution Systems (MES), and Test Execution Systems (TES)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to learn new skills or adapt to new situations. Un-phased by challenges that go beyond the traditional comfort zone or work experience. Multidisciplinary approach to problem solving&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with high project ownership under technical and schedule pressure, particularly where the scope and definition are limited&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience testing and operating with or around hazardous systems (high voltage up to 400V)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on projects that involve the integration of electrical, mechanical, and software/firmware systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with NixOS, or anydeclarative-configuration background (Ansible, Puppet, Chef).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Test frameworks — pytest-based harnesses, LabVIEW, TestStand or equivalent. Exposure to more than one is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The salary range for this role is an estimate based on a wide range of compensation factors, inclusive of base salary only. Actual salary offer may vary based on (but not limited to) work experience, education and/or training, critical skills, and/or business considerations. Highly competitive equity grants are included in the majority of full time offers; and are considered part of Anduril&#39;s total compensation package. Additionally, Anduril offers top-tier benefits for full-time employees, including:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;At Anduril, we invest in our people. Our comprehensive, competitive benefits package (available at little to no cost to employees) ensures you’re supported in health, recovery, and whatever comes next.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;For more information, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.anduril.com/careers&quot;&gt;Explore Our Benefits&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
