ering Waymo service across UK cities. This role works closely with Product, Operations Partnerships, Engineering, Global Operations, Ops Planning, Finance, Safety, Policy and business partners.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;We are seeking a confident, decisive, and results-oriented leader to join our team as a Supply Operations Manager. This role demands an individual who thrives in fast-paced, dynamic environments, excels at managing cross-functional teams, and is committed to driving operational success and market excellence for our autonomous ride-hailing service. You&#39;ll foster strong partnerships, champion continuous improvement, and leverage data analytics to monitor market health, identify trends, and implement proactive strategies to balance demand and supply, ultimately driving innovation and long-term success.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;In this hybrid role, you will report to the &lt;strong&gt;Country Lead within the European Market Operations Team.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic Leadership (Partner Support/Management): Strategic and decisive leadership to manage and optimize daily partner operations, fostering a high-performance culture emphasizing collaboration and accountability, escalating product issues while supporting partner multi-facility operations (partner results) to ensure strict adherence to all safety, compliance, and regulatory protocols.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercialization: Primary liaison to support internal stakeholders in expanding the market by providing guidance and expertise, communicating with all stakeholders to ensure alignment, monitoring progress, identifying potential issues, and developing contingency plans to ensure the success and sustainability of the market scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supply &amp;amp; Demand Planning: Manage Supply &amp;amp; Demand Planning by ensuring that staffing levels align with operational needs and in-service supply.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuous Improvement: Must be continuously monitoring and improving processes, systems, and performance metrics to drive efficiency and productivity, and reduce costs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Co-Lead Market Expansion: Strategically expand the market by executing innovative initiatives with partners, leveraging data insights, and applying critical thinking to identify opportunities and resolve challenges effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build Collaborative Partnerships: Build and maintain strong partnerships across the company and with partners, ensuring alignment with organizational standards, goals, and a shared commitment to success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive Sustainable Outcomes: Serve as a trusted leader with a continuous improvement mindset, consistently monitoring and enhancing processes, systems, and performance metrics to drive operational excellence, strengthen stakeholder alignment, and deliver measurable, sustainable results, all while boosting efficiency, productivity, and reducing costs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maximize Market Profitability: Manage departmental budgets, identifying and implementing cost-saving initiatives, and monitoring key performance indicators to effectively allocate resources and ensure all operational initiatives align with financial parameters and organizational goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in operations management, preferably managing daily operations in a fast-paced environment in fleet management, transportation, or logistics, with a deep understanding of safety.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree, or in lieu of a degree, an additional 6+ years of work experience in a combination of program management, business operations, strategy consulting, planning, or equivalent fields.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent leadership skills, including the ability to motivate &amp;amp; lead by influence partner teams, develop and execute strategies, and drive performance improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to deal with multiple conflicting priorities and stakeholder issues while driving towards pragmatic decisions/actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills to identify and address performance issues proactively, preferably using data analytics tools and reporting software to track key metrics and performance trends.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and presentation skills showcasing an ability to influence people to contribute to continuous improvement of operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We prefer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Ride-Hail &amp;amp; Transportation: Direct experience in the ride-hailing or broader transportation industry is a significant plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-Driven Decision Making: Proficiency in leveraging data analytics and reporting tools to monitor market health and inform strategic decisions is essential. Experience with SQL and data mining is highly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operational Management Experience: A background in general operations management, vendor management in addition to the minimum requirements, would be beneficial.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuous Improvement Mindset: A demonstrated history of identifying and implementing process improvements to increase efficiency and reduce costs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic &amp;amp; Decisive Leadership: The ability to provide clear, strategic leadership and make quick decisions in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The expected base salary range for this full-time position is listed below. Actual starting pay will be based on job-related factors, including exact work location, experience, relevant training and education, and skill level.&amp;nbsp; Waymo employees are also eligible to participate in Waymo’s discretionary annual bonus program, equity incentive plan, and generous Company benefits program, subject to eligibility requirements. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;£92,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;£96,500 GBP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/waymo/senior-supply-specialist-uk-london-383576","tags":["RHO - Market Mgmt (GWE)"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1793127324},{"slug":"senior-regional-ride-hail-ops-infra-specialist-europe-london-361878","company_name":"Waymo","title":"Senior Regional Ride-Hail Ops Infra Specialist - Europe","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Waymo is an autonomous driving technology company with the mission to be the world&#39;s most trusted driver. Since its start as the Google Self-Driving Car Project in 2009, Waymo has focused on building the Waymo Driver—The World&#39;s Most Experienced Driver™—to improve access to mobility while saving thousands of lives now lost to traffic crashes. The Waymo Driver powers Waymo’s fully autonomous ride-hail service and can also be applied to a range of vehicle platforms and product use cases. The Waymo Driver has provided over ten million rider-only trips, enabled by its experience autonomously driving over 100 million miles on public roads and tens of billions in simulation across 15+ U.S. states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Europe Operations team is accountable for service delivery and eliminating supply blockers to meet demand, working closely with technical program managers, facility engineers, and site operations leaders dedicated to building and sustaining the world&#39;s most advanced autonomous fleet infrastructure. We&amp;nbsp; bridge physical engineering, power grid delivery, and software tooling to ensure Waymo&#39;s fleet operates safely, efficiently and continuously at global scale.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this hybrid role, you will report to the &lt;strong&gt;Director of Operations, Head of Europe Operations&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Orchestrate European Site &amp;amp; Infrastructure Enablement: Lead the end-to-end multi-country program execution for new facility bring-up, high-voltage EV charging grid interconnections, and tech deployment across European hubs, ensuring infrastructure resilience and readiness for multi-market autonomous fleet operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive Scalable Automation &amp;amp; Process Architecture: Standardize depot workflows across European facilities enabling scale &amp;amp; fleet growth, using continuous improvement principles, tracking mitigations, and removing blockers for scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complex Program Management: Establish and enforce a unified framework for rider-only operations, driving decisions to unlock all types of infra required to deliver service, including parking, charging, pit-stops, service centers and testing locations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive Vendor &amp;amp; Strategic Supplier Governance: Establish strategic new and existing partner frameworks and requirements across Europe to deliver high-performing SLA adherence, CapEx efficiencies, and continuous service delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build High-Impact Cross-Functional Alignment: Serve as the strategic bridge between Facilities, Engineering and Product leadership and local European field teams, aligning international program goals with technical roadmap requirements and regional operational realities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize Multi-Country CapEx/OpEx Portfolios: Lead multi-million Euro infrastructure and technology budgets, establishing resource allocation models, cost-efficiency benchmarks, and financial governance to ensure European market expansion meets strategic financial targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience leading complex programs, technology operations, or infra-structure/industrial program management across multiple facilities, including multi-country European expansion in transportation or other operating fields/automated logistics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record as a senior technical, program management or strategy involving infrastructure, real estate bring-up, or large-scale technical operations across European regulatory jurisdictions (e.g., UK, Germany, Spain, France).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced expertise in data-driven operations management, using large sets of data to drive decision making, business intelligence, and advanced metrics to track multi-site throughput, charger utilization rates, and operational resilience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience developing and executing multi-facility Business Continuity Plans (BCP) and crisis recovery frameworks across high-demand critical facilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Engineering, Supply Chain, Business Operations, or equivalent practical experience (Master&#39;s/MBA or Six Sigma Black Belt preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication and executive stakeholder management skills with proven ability to influence matrixed cross-functional teams and external regulatory/utility entities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel within the EU up to 40% of the time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We prefer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Autonomous Mobility &amp;amp; EV Infrastructure Domain Expertise: Deep familiarity with AV fleet operations, or ride-hailing support systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-Border Regulatory Leadership: Hands-on experience navigating EU/UK transportation frameworks, municipal zoning, and high-voltage electrical grid interconnections with national utility providers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;International Program Scaling: Demonstrated success scaling operational footprints from initial pilot programs to multi-city commercial operations across diverse language and legal environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Systems Engineering &amp;amp; Automation Integration: Experience specifying, deploying, and validating programmatic software tools and automation systems inside physical depot environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in European Languages: Professional fluency in German, Spanish, French or other western European languages in addition to English is a strong advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lean/Six Sigma Certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The expected base salary range for this full-time position is listed below. Actual starting pay will be based on job-related factors, including exact work location, experience, relevant training and education, and skill level.&amp;nbsp; Waymo employees are also eligible to participate in Waymo’s discretionary annual bonus program, equity incentive plan, and generous Company benefits program, subject to eligibility requirements. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;£118,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;£124,000 GBP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/waymo/senior-regional-ride-hail-ops-infra-specialist-europe-london-361878","tags":["RHO - Market Mgmt (GWE)"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1793127324},{"slug":"insurance-operations-manager-london-323550","company_name":"Zego","title":"Insurance Operations Manager","description":"<h2><strong>About Zego 🚀</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Zego, we're on a mission to do the good thing, not the insurance thing.<br /><br />Insurance hasn't changed much in over a century. The way we live, work and travel has. We're building the real-time, AI-driven infrastructure that powers innovative insurance, so good drivers get cover that works the way they actually drive.<br /><br /><strong>We're not just updating insurance; We're leading the AI evolution in insurance </strong>🤖</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For us, AI isn't a line on a roadmap or a buzzword on a slide. It's our operating reality, and it's how we build products that back drivers instead of the old insurance playbook.<br /><br />We don't do things slowly, and we don't do bureaucracy. We back high-performance builders who want ownership, early responsibility and the chance to do the most career-defining work of their lives. You'll get the space to try things, the tools to move fast, and the room to see your ideas reach millions of drivers.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Do not take our word for it. Read what Zegons say about us on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.glassdoor.co.uk/Overview/Working-at-Zego-Insurance-EI_IE1851459.11,25.htm"><u>Glassdoor</u></a>.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you're ready to build the future of insurance,<strong> we're hiring.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Zego Insurance Limited (ZIL) is a Gibraltar-based motor insurer regulated by the GFSC. We're growing, and as we do, we need to keep maturing how we operate as an insurer - proportionate to our size, with strong governance and a firm regulatory focus. This is a pivotal role to help us do that in a scalable and sustainable way.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reporting into the Executive Director, Insurance Operations, you'll own ZIL's operations and lead insurer-focused projects across the business. You'll make sure we operate effectively as an insurer, bring more of our regulatory and project delivery in-house, and help us get ready for the bigger initiatives and partnerships ahead.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll also be involved in the management and oversight of our insurance partners and outsourced service providers, helping make sure the right operating rhythms are in place and contractual and regulatory requirements are met.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Here's what you'll be doing</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead insurer-focused projects and regulatory workstreams, such as onboarding new insurance partners, operational resilience and GFSC deliverables.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be hands-on in delivery. The expectation is to get things done and see them through to completion, not just oversee or track progress.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take ownership of ZIL's operational resilience framework, as well as business continuity and disaster recovery, keeping them embedded and aligned to regulatory expectations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support ZIL's internal audit programme, coordinating reviews, working with the business on findings and making sure actions are closed out.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Further enhance ZIL's governance, strengthening our frameworks and controls, proactively documenting procedures and keeping policies up to date, clearly owned and on their review cycle.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the oversight of our outsourced service providers, including Zego MGA. This includes maintaining our outsourcing register, due diligence and exit plans for critical providers, keeping intragroup agreements and service schedules up to date, and producing SLA and KPI reporting for committees.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the management of our insurance partners, ensuring effective operating rhythms, strong relationships and that contractual requirements are met.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Continually improve how we operate, simplifying processes and making the most of AI and the right tools to drive us forward.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll need to be successful in the role</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in an operations, project or governance role within a regulated insurer. Knowledge of Gibraltar, UK or EU insurance regulation is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A solid understanding of how an insurer works, such as co-insurance, reinsurance or MGA oversight.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of delivering complex projects across multiple teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with governance, policies or audit. Operational resilience experience is a bonus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong stakeholder management, both internally and with external partners.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Detail-oriented, proactive and good at solving problems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Able to prioritise and manage multiple workstreams in a structured way.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A hands-on go-getter who balances commercial, operational and regulatory needs.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The Zego ways of working 🏡</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Teams work better with time to collaborate and space to get things done. We call it Zego Hybrid: some of us are in our office (central London or Halifax) weekly, others monthly or quarterly. It's about finding the balance between face time and focus that produces great work and a healthy life around it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We also make a point of getting everyone in the same room. Teams come together every quarter, and once a year the whole company does, properly. It's a serious investment and consistently one of the best parts of the year.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QKOYDx6AMxQ"><u>Here is what the last one looked like</u></a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Benefits 🎁</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">💰 Market-competitive salary, benchmarked against your function and reviewed every year.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🏆 Annual performance bonus, linked to company performance and your contribution.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">📈 Share options, a real stake in the company and a share in the future you build</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🩺 Private medical insurance.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🏖️ Pension, generous holiday, and £1,000 a year to spend on getting to the office or learning something new.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">💻 Cutting-edge systems and tools, so you always have what you need to drive your impact.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? We want to hear from you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Zego, leading the AI evolution in insurance.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Equal opportunities 🌈</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We're an equal opportunity employer and we value diversity at our company. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, or disability status.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/zego/insurance-operations-manager-london-323550","tags":["Insurance"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1793126437},{"slug":"ai-ops-engineer-business-operations-london-137028","company_name":"Kernel","title":"AI Ops Engineer (Business Operations)","description":"<h2>About Kernel</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Agents are starting to sell, buy and operate on behalf of companies. But before an agent can close a deal, qualify an account, route a lead or assess risk, it has to answer a basic question: which company is this?</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today, that answer is messy, and no one answers it reliably. Business identity lives across CRMs, ERPs and third-party datasets full of duplicates, missing parent companies, stale addresses and incorrect enrichment. The cost shows up across the enterprise: sales teams miss revenue opportunities because they lack the right account context; operations teams take on avoidable exposure because risk signals are fragmented or wrong; and finance teams end up chasing, writing off, or defaulting on bad debt that should have been caught earlier.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Humans have worked around that mess for years. Agents cannot. They need a reliable business identity layer they can trust.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Kernel is building that layer: the business registry for agents. We issue a permanent Kernel ID for every business, plus the context an agent needs to act on it. Ops, data and revenue teams at <strong>Gong, Legora, Mistral, Canva and Notion</strong> already use Kernel on their own systems. Agents are next, and there will be far more of them.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We have raised $20M from top VCs and operators at Plaid, OpenAI, Slack and others, and we are growing 10x YoY.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>The Role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for an AI Ops Engineer to build the internal systems that help Kernel scale without adding unnecessary manual work. You’ll work across GTM, Marketing, Customer Success and Operations - finding the highest-leverage problems and building practical AI-powered workflows.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a hands-on builder role. You’ll take ideas from a vague business problem to a tool or workflow that people use, then maintain and improve it in production. You’ll choose the fastest sensible approach for each problem - coding agents, automation platforms, APIs, data pipelines or lightweight code.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll report to <strong>Arvin Ashrafi, Head of Finance &amp; Operations</strong>, and partner closely with GTM, Marketing, and Customer Success leadership.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What You’ll Be Doing</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Define how an AI-native company operates:</strong> help build Kernel’s internal playbook for using AI across GTM, Marketing, Customer Success and Operations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Make our GTM team more productive:</strong> automate the repetitive work in prospecting, account research, meeting prep and CRM hygiene, so BDRs, AEs and Account Managers spend more time with customers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build internal tools and workflows:</strong> use coding agents, APIs, automation platforms, no-code tools or lightweight code</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Turn company data into operational leverage:</strong> connect and improve data across our systems, then put it to work in AI agents, proactive workflows and better decision-making</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Put AI agents to work across Kernel:</strong> give teams agents with the right context, tools and guardrails so they can move faster without sacrificing judgement or reliability</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Be Kernel’s own internal customer:</strong> deploy Kernel on Kernel’s CRM, improve our GTM data and turn what you learn into useful feedback for Product and Engineering</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Level up the team:</strong> help colleagues become confident AI users, document what works and turn successful experiments into repeatable ways of working</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Your First 6 Months</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">For your first six months, you’ll focus on our sales team. You’ll sit with our BDRs, AEs and Account Managers and learn how they work day to day. Then you’ll automate everything that doesn’t need a human. That means going deep on Salesforce and our GTM stack, and owning the RevOps workflows behind them. After that, you’ll bring the same approach to Marketing, Customer Success and Operations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What You Bring</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A track record of shipping:</strong> you’ve built tools, automations or AI workflows that people use every day, ideally inside a small, fast-moving startup. Around 2–5 years of experience is typical, but what you’ve built matters more than your years. Ex-founders welcome</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experience inside a high-growth startup,</strong> or building your own, is highly desirable</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Curious about sales:</strong> you’re keen to learn how our BDRs and AEs work, and how Salesforce is set up, before you build for them</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI-tool obsessed:</strong> you are constantly testing new models, agents, MCPs and workflows, and you have the judgement to turn them into reliable systems that people actually adopt</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong data instincts:</strong> you can turn fragmented, messy information into reliable workflows and create feedback loops that keep it trustworthy</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Can’t unsee inefficiency:</strong> you see the company as a connected system; when you find a broken or unnecessarily manual process, your instinct is to understand it, build the fix and make sure it sticks</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>⚠️ This role may not be for you if you:</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Prefer deep specialization over breadth:</strong> this role means switching between projects and teams, depending on business needs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Prefer steady-state work over project-based sprints:</strong> priorities will shift as the business evolves</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Only want “strategic” work:</strong> you will personally build the tools, clean the data and fix the workflows</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>❌ This role is definitely not for you if you:</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Need every task to be clearly scoped before starting:</strong> ambiguity and learning on the fly are constant</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Avoid operational grunt work</strong> or lose interest after the prototype</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Want to protect a 9-to-6 or a mostly remote setup:</strong> we are in the office together 4–5 days a week and the pace is high</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What We Offer</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We will do our best to offer you a ride of a lifetime. It will not be easy, but it will be thrilling.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">💰 <strong>Salary:</strong> £60,000–£85,000 + equity</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🗓️ 24 days holiday per year + bank holidays</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🥕 £450 monthly office dinner allowance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">✈️ 2 weeks work-from-anywhere</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🍼 Generous parental leave policy</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">💼 Pension plan</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">💻 Top-spec equipment and central London office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🎉 Team events and dinners</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🚀 Work directly with the founders to deploy AI across a fast-growing company</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🏆 High-autonomy, high-trust environment with a small team shipping at pace</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>❤️ Team</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Arvin Ashrafi, Head of Finance &amp; Operations</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Amin Shafi, BizOps Associate</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Dave Bentham, Head of Sales</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>🎫 Visas &amp; Relocation</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Not offered for this role.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Interview Process</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Stage 1:</strong> <strong>Screening -</strong> Intro call</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Stage 2:</strong> <strong>Technical -</strong> In-person case interview</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Stage 3:</strong> <strong>Coffee chat -</strong> In-person discussion with members of our GTM team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Final Stage: Values -</strong> Interview with founders for culture and values alignment</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">If there is mutual fit, we move to references and offer.</p><hr><p>Compensation: £60K – £85K • Offers Equity</p><ul><li> • Base Salary £60K – £85K • Offers Equity</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/kernel/ai-ops-engineer-business-operations-london-137028","tags":["Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1793126437},{"slug":"engineering-leader-london-451279","company_name":"Kernel","title":"Engineering Leader","description":"<h2>About Kernel</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Agents are starting to sell, buy and operate on behalf of companies. But before an agent can close a deal, qualify an account, route a lead or assess risk, it has to answer a basic question: which company is this?</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today, that answer is messy, and no one answers it reliably. Business identity lives across CRMs, ERPs and third-party datasets full of duplicates, missing parent companies, stale addresses and incorrect enrichment. The cost shows up across the enterprise: sales teams miss revenue opportunities because they lack the right account context; operations teams take on avoidable exposure because risk signals are fragmented or wrong; and finance teams end up chasing, writing off, or defaulting on bad debt that should have been caught earlier.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Humans have worked around that mess for years. Agents cannot. They need a reliable business identity layer they can trust.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Kernel is building that layer: the business registry for agents. We issue a permanent KERN ID for every business, plus the context an agent needs to act on it. Ops, data and revenue teams at <strong>Gong, Legora, Mistral, Canva and Checkout</strong> already use Kernel on their own systems. Agents are next, and there will be far more of them.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We have raised <strong>$20M </strong>from <strong>top VCs and operators at Plaid, OpenAI, Slack and others, and we are growing 5x YoY.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll be a player-coach engineering leader with a spike in technical strategy, you'll own engineering delivery for your team end-to-end - from developing exceptional engineers to solving some of our most difficult engineering problems &amp; setting technical direction.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a hands-on leadership role. You'll spend roughly 20% of your time contributing code and 80% leading your team, with that ratio shifting as we scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build, hire, and develop a high-performing engineering team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help 