ne who both directs and who is hands on. It spans print, digital, environmental and presentation design rather than specialising in one, and it serves the whole company - sales, government relations, recruitment and the executive team, not marketing alone.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It is also where visual consistency is held. External agencies, photographers, 3D artists and film-makers deliver into the UFORCE brand; the Art Director sets what they work to and judges what comes back. The standard is that everything the company puts in front of a customer reads as though it came from one place.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you will do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design the materials the company sells and speaks with: capability collateral, specification sheets, presentations, launch assets, digital and social graphics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help evolve the UFORCE visual system - typography, colour, layout, iconography and the treatment of platform imagery - and keep it documented well enough that others can work to it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn technical material - system architectures, concepts of operation, platform diagrams - into images a non-specialist can understand.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design exhibition and event graphics, from stand panels to printed handouts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Art-direct photography, film and 3D work, on location and in review, so that commissioned material comes back usable and on-brand.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Active use of AI tools in how work is run and delivered, and an appetite to commission or build workflows that do not yet exist rather than wait for them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Direct localisation of work across the company's markets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Apply the company's security and export-control requirements to visual material, and route imagery of platforms, facilities and personnel for clearance before release.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>Required Skills</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Substantial experience as a Graphic designer or art director, in-house or in an agency, with a portfolio showing both range and finished craft across print, digital and environmental work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Command of typography, hierarchy and composition, and a body of work that holds to a consistent system rather than a collection of one-off styles.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to art-direct others - photographers, film-makers, illustrators, 3D artists - from written brief through review to delivery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep fluency in Figma, the company's primary design environment: components, variants and shared libraries, not frames alone. Working knowledge of InDesign and Illustrator for print and large-format work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Willingness to master Google Slides. Presentations are a primary sales instrument.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience making complex or technical subject matter legible, in any field - engineering, science, medicine, infrastructure or defence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Eligibility to gain UK security clearance</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience designing for defence, dual-use or engineering-led products</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technical illustration, diagramming or 3D</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Motion design or video editing</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The nature of combat has changed.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tomorrow’s battlefield success depends on autonomy, speed, and adaptability.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">And UFORCE is ready.