promising: no document that overclaims, no adjective that would not survive a procurement review. The narrative is expected to iterate at the pace of the products.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you will do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own positioning and messaging for products, and maintain the frameworks that keep it consistent across markets, languages and audiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Produce the materials the company sells with: one-pagers, capability briefs, specification sheets, sales decks, demonstration narratives and launch content.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain a current assessment of the competitive landscape - the neo-primes, the incumbent primes and the low-cost entrants - and convert it into positioning rather than description.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Brief designers, 3D artists and film-makers so that a complex system is legible visually.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide PR, communications and government relations with the product substance their work depends on, and ensure claims remain consistent wherever they appear.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead go-to-market for new products and capabilities, covering audience, message, materials, sequencing and timing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Travel to events, facilities and customer engagements.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Required Skills</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Substantial experience marketing hardware or software within a technology company, including ownership of at least one launch from positioning through to market.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated ability to translate complex technical concepts into clear, compelling narratives without loss of accuracy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional writing and editing across registers. Copy for engineers, procurement, investors and press are four distinct disciplines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to brief a creative such that the resulting image or video explains a system rather than decorating it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A record of cross-functional work with product and engineering teams, and a willingness to keep asking elementary questions until the answer is clear.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to obtain UK national security clearance if required</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>Nice to have</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in defence, dual-use or uncrewed systems, whether in industry or in service</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with engineering or operational teams remotely</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Complementary skills in design or video</p></li></ul><h2></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The nature of combat has changed.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tomorrow’s battlefield success depends on autonomy, speed, and adaptability.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">And UFORCE is ready.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are You?</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/uforce/senior-product-marketing-manager-london-34988","tags":["Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"United Kingdom - London","created_at":1793126436},{"slug":"video-producer-editor-london-391061","company_name":"Uforce","title":"Video Producer & Editor","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">UFORCE exists to make aggression unaffordable.<br /><br />Founded in Ukraine and headquartered in London, UFORCE is a defence-technology company with operations across Europe, the United States and Asia.<br /><br />UFORCE builds uncrewed vessels, ground robotics and aircraft, autonomy software, and the command-and-control layer that operates them together. Each platform is deployable on its own, and stronger as part of the system. Its product lines include the MAGURA family of uncrewed surface vessels, the NEMESIS family of strike platforms, the LIUT family of ground robotic platforms, and counter-UAS systems.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As the Video Producer &amp; Editor, you will be the point between raw footage and published work. The output goes onto company channels, into the hands of sales and government relations, and in front of closed-door audiences—including material that cannot leave the building.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Video is the clearest evidence of what UFORCE does to those outside the military. The systems are real, they are in use, and footage of them shows our customers what no render or animation can. In a market full of future-tense capability claims, that is the differentiator, and this role is what converts it into content people actually see.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is not an assembly role. You are expected to shape and direct content as well as cut it: to decide what is worth capturing, what the film is, and what to leave out. The register is real and observed rather than advertised. The standard is publishable as it leaves the timeline.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It is a mid-level role with unusual freedom. There is no post-production team and no producer. The work is daily, the subject matter is serious, and there is room for someone who wants to build their craft on material most editors never get near.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you will do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cut and finish film for company channels, social platforms, sales and government relations, and internal and closed-door audiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shape content from the outset: propose ideas, write shot lists and capture briefs, and direct or shoot capture where needed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deliver distinct cuts for distinct audiences rather than reformatting one film for all of them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Finish to a publishable standard—grade, sound, captioning, titling and versioning.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the footage library: cataloguing, archive structure, backup and version control.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hold the UFORCE film language and keep output consistent, including work delivered by external film-makers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Travel to facilities, ranges, events and deployments, sometimes at short notice, and film in industrial and field conditions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Utilise approved AI tools to optimize your workflow, strictly adhering to data security guidelines and ensuring no sensitive material leaves secure networks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Apply the company's security and export-control requirements to footage, and route material showing platforms, facilities and personnel for clearance before release.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Required Skills</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Around three to six years of professional editing experience, with a showreel of published work rather than showpieces.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Command of pacing, structure and sound, and the ability to explain the decisions behind a cut—particularly what was removed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in a factual, documentary, news or event register, not branded content alone.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Evidence of consistent output at pace, self-managed: media handling, versioning and deadlines without a producer.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A piece taken from idea and shot list through to final cut.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluency in a professional NLE—Premiere Pro, DaVinci Resolve or Final Cut—with working knowledge of After Effects or equivalent for basic motion work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sound judgement with confidential, embargoed or otherwise restricted material.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A point of view on what good looks like, and the willingness to argue for it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Right to work in the UK and eligibility to obtain UK Security Clearance (SC level).</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to Have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Camera operation to a publishable standard, including commercial drone operation (with CAA certification).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Motion graphics and titling beyond basics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stills photography.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience cutting technical or engineering subject matter.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in defence, dual-use or uncrewed systems, whether in industry or in service.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The nature of combat has changed.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tomorrow’s battlefield success depends on autonomy, speed, and adaptability.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">And UFORCE is ready.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are You?</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/uforce/video-producer-editor-london-391061","tags":["Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"United Kingdom - London","created_at":1793126436},{"slug":"staff-engineer-platform-tooling-london-295202","company_name":"Atominvest","title":"Staff Engineer - Platform & Tooling","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who is Atominvest</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Atominvest is the operating system for modern private markets asset managers. Our modular, flexible SaaS technology underpins key investor- and portfolio-management workflows.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our customers are sophisticated private equity, growth equity, and private credit firms managing billions in assets globally. We aim to deliver ongoing high-quality outcomes for them through a long-term partnership mindset.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Atominvest, you’ll be working on something very exciting: the future of work, investments and sustainability/ ethical investing for the world’s best investors and delivering a positive impact through this. Based on the growth we are experiencing, we think we’re on to something big.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It won’t be easy. Joining a scale up business is an amazing and rewarding challenge, pushing well beyond the boundaries of natural growth cycles. You’ll move quicker than feels comfortable and be brilliant at continually re-prioritizing what must get done to keep Atominvest growing year over year at the pace of the best SaaS companies on the planet.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’ve gone from zero to ten, now we’re looking to go from ten to one hundred!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>About the role</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hi, I'm Thomas, VP Engineering at Atominvest. This is the hire I'm most excited about, so I wanted to tell you about it myself.<br /><br />You'll own the platform our clients run on and build the AI development harness our engineers work in day to day. That work runs from infrastructure to application code, so we're looking for an experienced engineer with breadth across both, and depth in at least one. Together, it's what lets a small, lean team, working alongside AI agents, ship like a much bigger one.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">By platform, we mean everything our product and our engineers stand on: infrastructure, security, test automation, developer experience, and the agent pipelines that run through all of them. It's a broad, hands-on role. You'll write infrastructure as code for a new service one day and address network vulnerabilities the next, then enhance our AI development harness and release a new feature, all within the same month.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">You might be a platform engineer who loves shipping product, or a full-stack engineer who has run serious production infrastructure. Either works.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As deployments grow more complex, the team needs your depth in infrastructure and distributed systems. You'll strengthen the architecture and make the design decisions the platform will rest on for years. Those decisions should leave room to grow, because future products may bring much larger volumes of data than we handle today.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It has to stay dependable while we do it. Our software needs to be available around the clock, every day of the year, and data integrity is critical. Our clients use Atominvest to report to their own investors, so a wrong number matters as much as an outage. Security, reliability and audit-readiness matter too. If you enjoy getting those right without slowing everything else down, you'll find plenty of fun things to work on.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>The machine that builds the product</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're becoming AI-native. Agents do more and more of the mechanical work of writing code, and engineers build the machine that builds the product: the architecture, the specs, the limits agents work within, and the evals that tell us whether their output is right.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">I think that moves an engineer's leverage upstream. When code is cheap, the scarce things are judgement and understanding. Which problem is worth solving? What does good look like for the person using it? Is the output actually right? Did what we shipped help? The best engineers I've worked with always solved the end problem, with code as the medium. Now that's most of the job.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">That's why product and user understanding sit at the centre of how we work. An engineer who knows our clients' workflows can point agents at the right problem and spot when the result is subtly wrong. Without that, agents just build the wrong thing faster.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your part is the AI development harness that makes this safe. That means sandboxed environments with synthetic data, scoped and audited access to logs and alerts, and evals and validation gates in CI. It also means firm lines, enforced by tooling, that keep production deploys and secrets in human hands, and client data out of reach of development agents.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll also build the agent orchestration pipelines that run in three places: in how we build software, in AI workflows inside the product our clients use, and in the internal tools our implementation team uses to onboard and configure clients.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you'll do<br /></h2><h3>Build the machine that builds the product</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Most of your time goes here.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build our AI development harness.</strong> Self-service infrastructure, a reproducible development environment, and the sandboxes, guardrails and evals that let agents take on more of the work safely, with results we can measure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Automate quality.</strong> Build the QA automation pipeline: automated tests, validation gates and release checks that give us confidence in every change, including the ones agents write.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Orchestrate agents across the business.</strong> Build pipelines that run agents reliably and safely in our product workflows and our internal implementation tools, not just in engineering.</p></li></ul><h3>Own the platform</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own our infrastructure.</strong> We're migrating to ECS. You'll strengthen our ECS architecture, see the move through in safe, reversible stages, bring every resource under infrastructure as code, and retire the old deployment model.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build security into the platform.</strong> Tenant-scoped credentials, per-tenant secrets, least-privilege access, and the audit trail that SOC 2 and our clients' security teams expect.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Make production observable.</strong> Set up the monitoring, alerting and tracing we rely on, and build playbooks for on-call and incident response which is shared amongst the team.</p></li></ul><h3>Work across the stack</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Make the application changes the harness needs,</strong> such as synthetic data, test hooks and the specs agents work from.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ship product.</strong> Pick up application work in TypeScript and React alongside the team. Over time, you'll learn the codebase as well as the platform it runs on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Grow the team around you.</strong> Write the design notes and runbooks, pair with and review the work of other engineers, and mentor those who want to grow into infrastructure, so the platform never depends on one person.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>Your first six months</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Get the first parts of "the machine" running, and show that they make the team faster without lowering quality.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At the moment all of our end to end testing is done manually by our Product team. That's a massive manual overhead that bottlenecks our product development. You'll help build our AI-powered QA automation pipeline, so every change, whether a person or an agent wrote it, is tested automatically before it reaches clients.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strengthen the ECS architecture and complete the move with no disruption to clients.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Get the platform fully into code, with tenant isolation and least privilege designed in.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Put in place the monitoring and on-call foundations the team will build on.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>How you'll work</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll own this area rather than work through a ticket queue. You'll decide what to build and when it's good enough, write your decisions down so others can challenge them, and tell us when something isn't worth doing. You'll work closely with Product from the start of significant work, because the platform exists to serve clients and the engineers building for them.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You and I will work together every day. We'll shape the technical direction together and think through the hard calls, and you'll have a direct line to every decision that affects your work. I'll back your judgement, and I'll expect you to push back when you think I'm wrong.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is an individual contributor role, but we expect you to multiply the team: leading different areas at different times, and delivering through others as well as through your own work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>You'll probably enjoy this if</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'd rather build a platform properly than keep patching one.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're product-minded. You've probably worked at a startup or scale-up, or even founded something yourself. Seeing your work out in the world, solving real problems, is what motivates you. You ask who a change is for before you ask how to build it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You already work this way. Agents write much of your code, and your time goes on design, specs and judging the output. You've built AI tooling for yourself, and probably for others on your team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You get satisfaction from making other engineers faster.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're comfortable writing Terraform, an API endpoint and an answer to a client's security questionnaire in the same week.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've been the person others come to with hard problems, and you've changed your mind publicly when the evidence said so.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>This probably isn't for you if</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You want a pure DevOps or SRE role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You want to manage people right now. These opportunities might exist in the future, but for now we're small, lean and as flat as possible.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>What you'll bring</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Very few people match every line. If most of this describes you, we'd like to hear from you.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Deep, hands-on AWS.</strong> Several years running production workloads on ECS or EKS, with a solid grasp of IAM, networking and Lambda.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Infrastructure as code as a habit</strong>, with Terraform or CloudFormation, including bringing existing hand-built resources under code.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Scaling distributed systems.</strong> You've taken systems through real growth in load and data, and can teach others what you learnt.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Single-tenant SaaS experience.</strong> You know the isolation trade-offs and how to keep one client's data and credentials away from another's.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Security and compliance</strong> as part of engineering: least privilege, secrets management, and evidence for SOC 2 or ISO 27001.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Production experience:</strong> on-call, incidents, post-mortems, and observability tooling such as Datadog, Grafana or Honeycomb.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Full-stack product building.</strong> Senior TypeScript and Node.js, plus React, with a track record of shipping features end to end yourself, not just supporting the people who do.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Test automation and CI/CD.</strong> You've designed pipelines that test at the right levels and release safely, and you keep them fast and simple.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Tooling you've built for AI agents</strong>, not just used: agent configuration and orchestration, MCP servers or similar integrations, evals, automated review.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>Our stack</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">TypeScript, Node.js, React and MongoDB Atlas, running on AWS. CircleCI and Bitbucket. AI coding agents are part of everyday work. You don't need experience of all of these.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>How we hire</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We want to see how you actually work, so there are no whiteboard puzzles.</p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Screening call with me (20 minutes)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competencies interview with me (30 minutes)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technical deep dive with a few of our engineers (90 minutes)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Culture fit interview with our CEO, Hemal (30 minutes)</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em">I'll be your main point of contact throughout. You'll know what to expect before each stage, and if we don't make an offer, I'll give you feedback.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/atominvest/staff-engineer-platform-tooling-london-295202","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1793126436},{"slug":"senior-field-marketing-manager-emea-london-212402","company_name":"Assembledhq","title":"Senior Field Marketing Manager, EMEA","description":"<h2><strong>About Assembled</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assembled helps companies scale great customer support. As consumers, we’ve all been there. You need help, you’re stuck on hold or going in circles with an AI, and your problem still isn’t solved.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Behind great support is a complex operational problem: thousands of people and AI agents working across teams, time zones, and products as new problems emerge. Assembled gives support leaders the tools to manage that complexity, from AI agents that resolve customer issues to software that forecasts demand, builds schedules, and makes intraday adjustments.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">More than 400 companies, including DoorDash, Salesforce, Stripe, and Sephora, trust <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.assembled.com/customers">Assembled</a>. We've raised $71M from NEA, Emergence Capital, Stripe, and Basis Set Ventures and have offices in San Francisco, New York, and London.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>The Role</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re hiring our first marketer in London. Europe is our next growth market, and right now we’ve got a tight-knit, quota-focused sales team with big goals and not much regional marketing behind them—yet.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll change that. Field events are the engine — dinners, roadshows, conferences, executive gatherings that put our team in front of the CX and Workforce Management leaders running Europe’s most complex operations. But this isn’t a role that stops at the event calendar. You’ll be the person who figures out what the European market needs from marketing and then goes and does it.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re starting in the UK with plans to expand across the region. You’ll work closely with our global events lead on moments where EMEA shows up inside the worldwide program, and with our growth team on campaigns that need European flair.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work together in person five days a week from our London office in King’s Cross.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h3><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the EMEA field calendar and the budget behind it — decide which events, dinners, and roadshows are worth doing, and which ones we skip</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run field as a pipeline channel: pre-event targeting through opportunity creation and deal acceleration, with named accounts attached to every program</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build account-based programs sized to the deal, whether that's one account, a handful, or a roomful, in lockstep with the London sales team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build our EMEA partner and channel motion — joint events, co-marketing, and the relationships that get us in front of buyers we can't reach on our own</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be the voice of the European market inside Assembled: what needs localizing, which content doesn't land, where our story has to change by country, and what customer stories to bring to life</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Foster community efforts. Get to know the European CX/WFM community by genuinely contributing and building relationships across a wide variety of stakeholders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring EU-specific campaign ideas to the team and make sure Europe is designed into campaigns rather than translated at the end</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build AI workflows that let one marketer cover multiple countries — invite list enrichment, event pages, personalized follow-up at volume, post-event analysis</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h3><strong>What You Bring</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">6–9 years in field, events, or regional marketing at B2B companies selling into enterprise, including time owning UK or EMEA programs rather than supporting someone else's</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Startup, get sh*t done mindset. The region is new and our team there is small and scrappy. You know how to spot the highest-leverage opportunities and collaborate cross-functionally to make magic happen</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've been early somewhere — the first marketer in a region or on a small team, where no playbook existed and you wrote one</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Event judgment with receipts. Tell us about an event you cut and why, not only the ones that worked</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Nice to have: experience in European markets beyond the UK, with an understanding of how programs need to differ by market</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A close working relationship with sales. You've sat in pipeline reviews, you know what an AE needs from a dinner, and you can hold your own on account strategy</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI systems you've built and use, with an example you can walk through. One marketer covering this much ground without AI is a headcount request, not a plan</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A bias to go first. You'd rather run a twelve-person dinner next month than spend the quarter planning a conference booth for next year</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h3><strong>Our UK benefits</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Quarterly credits for professional development, wellness, and commuting</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Budget for AI tools and experimentation, giving you room to test new ideas, build workflows, and rethink how you work</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Paid parental leave</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Onsite work model with catered lunches everyday (M-F)</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>The estimated base salary range for this role is £80,000 - £105,000 per year. The base pay offered may vary depending on location, job-related knowledge, skills, and experience. Stock options are provided as part of the compensation package, in addition to a full range of medical, financial, and/or other benefits, dependent on the position offered.</em></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We know great candidates don’t always meet every requirement listed in a job description. If the role excites you and you believe you can make an impact at Assembled, we encourage you to apply. We value diverse perspectives and are committed to building an inclusive workplace where everyone feels like they belong and has the opportunity to do their best work. We look forward to hearing from you!</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>For United States Applicants:</em><br /><em>Assembled participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the United States.</em><br /><br /><em>For United Kingdom Applicants:</em><br /><em>Assembled is required to verify your right to work in the UK and will conduct a Right to Work check prior to employment in accordance with applicable law.</em></p><hr><p>Compensation: £80K – £105K • Offers Equity</p><ul><li> • Estimated base salary £80K – £105K • Offers Equity</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/assembledhq/senior-field-marketing-manager-emea-london-212402","tags":["Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London, UK","created_at":1793126435},{"slug":"sales-operations-business-partner-london-345688","company_name":"Pleo","title":"Sales Operations Business Partner","description":"<h2><strong>About Pleo</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Messy spend management is tricky business. And tedious processes are a lose-lose situation for all involved, not just finance. At Pleo, we're changing that. We build spend solutions that make managing money seamless, empowering, and surprisingly effective for finance teams and employees alike - with a vision to help all businesses ‘go beyond’.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The word ‘Pleo’ actually means ‘more than you’d expect’, and living by that mantra has been the secret to our success over the last 10 years.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Now, we’re at a pivotal moment in our journey; every move we make has a direct impact on our 40,000+ customers, our business, and our collective success. We need people who take pride in uncovering customer needs, who turn complex problems into simple solutions, challenge the way things are done (respectfully), and always aim high. With great ambitions driving us forward, we can’t say we’ve got this whole thing figured out. And frankly, that’s half the fun! What we can say is that we’re a driven, progressive, and, importantly, a kind bunch of 850+ people from over 100 nationalities, all committed to delivering the future of business spending, together.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for a Sales Operations Business Partner to sit between our sales leadership and the systems, data, and processes that run the revenue engine. You’ll help the sales team understand where deals stand, where revenue is coming from, and where it’s at risk. You’ll own how we track pipeline, report on performance, and build the dashboards leaders rely on to make decisions. This is a role for someone who thinks in business outcomes first and uses data and tools as the means to get there.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own pipeline management processes, including stage definitions, forecasting cadence, and hygiene standards, and work with sales managers to keep the pipeline accurate.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain regular sales reporting covering bookings, pipeline coverage, conversion rates, win/loss, and rep and team performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design, build, and maintain dashboards that give leadership and frontline managers a clear view of performance against targets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as a business partner to sales leaders: understand their priorities, translate them into operational requirements, and bring data-backed recommendations to planning and business reviews.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support forecasting and quarterly business reviews by preparing the data, challenging assumptions, and flagging risks early.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own day-to-day administration and configuration of the CRM (e.g. Salesforce or HubSpot), including fields, workflows, user access, and reporting structure, in partnership with the RevOps or systems team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive adoption of CRM and sales processes by working with managers and reps, and by making the right behaviour the easy one.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support territory, quota, and compensation-related analysis as needed, in partnership with Finance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify process gaps and inefficiencies across the sales funnel and lead improvements, documenting changes and training the team on them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work cross-functionally with Marketing, Finance, Customer Success, and Product Ops to keep data consistent across systems.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll bring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">7+ years of experience in sales operations, revenue operations, GTM operations, or a related commercial role, ideally in a [B2B SaaS / relevant industry] environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong experience with CRM systems, ideally Salesforce or HubSpot, including reporting and basic administration.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid understanding of sales metrics and funnel dynamics, including pipeline coverage, conversion, forecasting accuracy, and sales cycle length.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven ability to build clear reports and dashboards in tools such as Excel/Google Sheets, Looker, Tableau, or Power BI. You don’t need to write code, but you should be comfortable working with data and spotting what matters.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience running pipeline reviews or forecast calls, or supporting leaders who do.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A consultative approach: you can listen to a sales leader, ask the right questions, and turn their needs into a practical solution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong communication skills, with the ability to present findings clearly to senior stakeholders and explain trade-offs simply.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Good judgement and attention to detail, with the ability to balance speed and accuracy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable operating in a fast-paced environment with multiple priorities.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience supporting a sales team through a scaling or transformation phase.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with sales compensation or territory planning tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exposure to revenue analytics or forecasting methodologies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with a BI tool or basic SQL, though this is not required.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What success looks like</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Leadership trusts the pipeline and forecast numbers and uses them to make decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sales managers run their reviews from the dashboards you’ve built, without needing manual reports.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">CRM data quality improves measurably over time.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sales leaders see you as a partner who brings ideas, not just reports.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>About your application</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>English first.</strong> Since it's our company language, please submit your application in English. You’ll be using it a lot if you join us.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A fair look for everyone.</strong> Our talent team reads every single application to ensure the process is fair. To keep things running smoothly, we only accept applications through our system—our support team can’t pass on calls or emails.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Diversity drives us.</strong> We can only reach our goals if our team reflects the world around us. That starts with you hitting apply, even if you don't tick every single box. We encourage people from all backgrounds and experiences to join us.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Interview at your best.</strong> We want you to feel comfortable throughout the process. If you have any accessibility requirements or need a specific format, email ----- We’ll design a process that works for you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your data is safe.</strong> When you apply, we process your personal data as a data processor. For more information on how Pleo processes personal data, read our Privacy Policy <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="in-cell-link" href="https://www.pleo.io/en/legal"><u>here</u></a>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Applying for multiple roles?</strong> Nothing is stopping you, and we assess every role independently. However, we do look for alignment, so make sure you can explain why your interest and experience are right for each specific role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Reapplying.</strong> If you’re applying for the same role again, please wait six months from your last decision before hitting submit.</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/pleo/sales-operations-business-partner-london-345688","tags":["Revenue Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1793126434},{"slug":"product-engineer-design-engineering-knowledge-cambridge-261481","company_name":"Neuralconcept","title":"Product Engineer | Design Engineering Knowledge","description":"<h1>Product Engineer | Design Engineering Knowledge</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location:</strong> Cambridge (UK), hybrid with up to 2 remote days per week</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team:</strong> Product</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Start date:</strong> ASAP</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>About Neural Concept</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Neural Concept is the engineering intelligence platform used by leading manufacturers in automotive, aerospace, and energy. We combine geometric and physics AI with LLM-based agents so engineering teams can move from customer requirements to validated designs in a fraction of the usual time.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>About the role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design decisions depend on information that lives outside the CAD model: customer requirements, design rules, manufacturing and assembly constraints, and cost targets. This information is spread across specification documents, handbooks, ERP systems, requirements management tools, and system models. Engineers gather it by hand, often late in the process, and conflicts surface at design reviews or on the production line.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We call the capability that closes this gap Design Engineering Knowledge. It connects the design to the information ecosystem around it, so requirements, constraints, and trade-offs are available to engineers and AI agents while they work on the design itself.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Product Engineer, you will build this capability. Requirements are the first focus area: extracting them from customer specifications and requirements management systems, structuring them, and keeping them traceable. You will then extend the same foundation to design rule checks, Design for Manufacturing (DfM), Design for Assembly (DfA), and Design for Cost, and connect it to the enterprise systems where this knowledge already lives.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will work with the Product Manager, solution engineers, and customer engineering teams, as the primary developer from the first customer conversation to the version running in production.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you will do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the requirements foundation: ingest customer specifications and RFQ packages, extract requirements with LLM and agent-based pipelines, and keep each one traceable to its source document and page.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Extend this foundation to design rules, DfM, DfA, and Design for Cost, turning standards, handbooks, and company know-how into constraints that software and agents can use.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring requirements, constraints, and trade-offs into the design workflow, so engineers can check a design against them at any stage and see which ones apply to the part they are working on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build integrations with the systems around the design: requirements management systems, ERP (cost, materials, and supplier data), and system design and MBSE tools for architecture and system-level requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design the data model that links requirements, rules, and constraints to parts, design parameters, and simulation results.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create evaluation sets and quality metrics with customers, so extraction and checking accuracy is measured and improves with every release.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design human-in-the-loop review flows where engineers validate and edit AI output, with versioning and a full audit trail.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Spot recurring patterns across customers and turn them into reusable components of the Neural Concept platform.</p></li></ul><h2>Who you are</h2><h3>Must have</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building and shipping production Python software in fast-moving, cross-functional teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with LLM applications in production: structured outputs, retrieval-augmented generation, agents, and evaluation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience integrating with enterprise systems through APIs and data models, for example ERP, PLM, or requirements management tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with document processing, such as PDF parsing, OCR, or information extraction.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong software practices: testing (pytest), CI, packaging, code review, and git.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A product mindset. You talk to users, understand the problem before writing code, and ship in small, measurable steps.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear, concise communication with both customer engineers and internal teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Based in Cambridge (UK) or willing to relocate.</p></li></ul><h3>Nice to have</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Background in mechanical engineering or physics, with exposure to DfM, DfA, or design-to-cost practices.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with requirements engineering and model-based systems engineering (MBSE, SysML).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with CAD data or geometry processing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with vision-language models, vector databases, or search ranking.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you get</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ownership of a product capability that customers use in real engineering programs, with direct access to the engineers who use it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A competitive salary and rewarding opportunities as we continue to scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A collaborative, multicultural team where your work is visible and recognized.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Colleagues who share knowledge freely and support each other.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A hybrid model and flexible hours. We focus on results and trust you to organize your time.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h3>We're proud to be an equal opportunity employer, and we're committed to building a diverse and inclusive environment where you can thrive. </h3><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/neuralconcept/product-engineer-design-engineering-knowledge-cambridge-261481","tags":["Product"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Cambridge","created_at":1793126433},{"slug":"fractional-product-lead-3-month-contract-london-290448","company_name":"Bike Club","title":"Fractional Product Lead - 3 month contract","description":"<p><strong>We're customer obsessed. We put the customer at the heart of everything we do - and we're looking for people who feel the same way.</strong></p><h3><strong>About Bike Club</strong></h3><p>Bike Club is the easiest way to keep kids on the right sized bike. Through our subscription model, we remove the hassle of buying, outgrowing and reselling children's bikes, so families always have the right bike, right when they need it. We are a purpose led, fast-growing business built on ease, care, progress and joy - with a relentless focus on customer growth, retention and building a more circular approach to children's cycling.</p><h3><strong>Role Summary and Engagement</strong></h3><p>Bike Club is looking for a fractional Product Lead to lead the member product, turn customer needs and commercial priorities into a clear direction and a prioritised roadmap, and deliver measurable improvements. The role combines senior Product leadership with practical discovery and delivery coordination in a lean team.</p><p>The Product Lead will also establish an AI-enabled Product function, using AI to speed up customer insight, discovery, prototyping and experimentation. They will identify where AI and automation can improve the member experience or business efficiency, and turn the strongest opportunities into prioritised, measurable initiatives.</p><p>This is a part-time fixed-term employment or freelance contract estimated at 3 days per week for a period of 3 months.</p><h3><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></h3><ul><li><p><strong>Product direction and roadmap:</strong> own the direction and roadmap across the member lifecycle: joining, managing a subscription, ongoing membership, exchange and retention. Balance member value with operational efficiency, cost and business priorities.</p></li><li><p><strong>Discovery:</strong> lead discovery with members and colleagues across Marketing, Customer Service, Operations and markets. Use research, behavioural data and service insight to define problems before committing to solutions.</p></li><li><p><strong>Lifecycle and retention:</strong> work jointly with Marketing and the retention owner on lifecycle journeys, retention initiatives, experiments and shared measures. Product owns the supporting experience and requirements. Marketing owns campaign and channel execution.</p></li><li><p><strong>Requirements and backlog:</strong> turn agreed priorities into clear requirements, user stories and acceptance criteria. Maintain one prioritised product backlog, including operational improvements and approved AI or automation initiatives.</p></li><li><p><strong>Investment cases:</strong> build proportionate cases for investment, setting out expected benefits, cost, dependencies and how outcomes will be measured. Recommend stopping or deferring work where value is insufficient.</p></li><li><p><strong>Delivery:</strong> agree delivery commitments with Engineering using realistic estimates and available capacity. Coordinate stakeholders, adoption and launches with the combined QA and Delivery role, keeping risks and changes visible.</p></li><li><p><strong>Marketing autonomy:</strong> support Marketing with appropriate content, landing-page and experimentation capabilities. Agree the boundary between the member product, CRM and support tools.</p></li><li><p><strong>AI in Product work:</strong> use AI routinely for research synthesis, analysis, requirements development, prototyping and experiment design, and validate findings against customer evidence.</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Prioritise valuable applications with Marketing, Customer Service, Operations and the Data and Automation function. Test assumptions and build proportionate business cases. Customer-service automation should support the wider member journey.</p></li><li><p>Share responsibility with Marketing for using AI to support lifecycle insight, proposition testing and retention experiments, with agreed measures of customer and commercial impact.</p></li></ul><ul><li><p><strong>Leave things in a better state:</strong> because the engagement is part-time and time-limited, document the roadmap, backlog, ways of working and AI approach so the team can continue without the Product Lead, and hand over clearly at the end.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Requirements</strong></h3><ul><li><p>Extensive Product Management experience including owning a digital product roadmap and delivering measurable customer and commercial improvements, preferably in a subscription, membership or related consumer business.</p></li><li><p>Strong discovery skills, including customer interviews, journey mapping, data interpretation, problem definition and testing assumptions before investment.</p></li><li><p>Commercial judgement: can compare value, effort, cost and risk, build practical investment cases and make clear prioritisation decisions.</p></li><li><p>Ability to lead across functions, challenge senior stakeholders constructively and maintain focus when priorities compete.</p></li><li><p>Experience working with Engineering, Design, Marketing, Customer Service and Operations through delivery, launch and continuous improvement.</p></li><li><p>Demonstrable experience embedding AI into Product workflows, with examples of faster learning, better decisions or reduced effort. Able to distinguish valuable AI applications from features that add unnecessary complexity.</p></li><li><p>Track record of working independently and effectively in a part-time, fractional or interim capacity, making visible progress in limited days a week.</p></li><li><p>Able to start quickly, and leave behind clear documentation and repeatable ways of working.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Measures Of Success</strong></h3><p>Baselines, numerical targets, data sources and review dates are agreed with the executive sponsor and relevant business owners within the first 30 days. Delivery and outcomes are reviewed weekly.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Member retention:</strong> improvement in the agreed retention or cancellation measure for targeted journeys, assessed jointly with Marketing and the retention owner.</p></li><li><p><strong>Member experience:</strong> improvement in self-service completion and reduction in avoidable support contact for prioritised journeys, without deterioration in customer experience.</p></li><li><p><strong>Conversion:</strong> improvement in agreed joining and exchange conversion measures, using experiments or comparable cohorts where practical.</p></li><li><p><strong>Speed of learning:</strong> reduced time from identifying a customer problem to testing a solution, with evidence that decisions remain grounded in customer insight.</p></li><li><p><strong>AI and automation:</strong> validated initiatives deliver agreed improvements in member experience, retention or operational efficiency, measured with the relevant business owner.</p></li><li><p><strong>Roadmap value:</strong> proportion of priority initiatives with a stated outcome, baseline and measurement plan before delivery, followed by a documented benefits review.</p></li><li><p><strong>Delivery confidence:</strong> performance against jointly agreed milestones, with changes in scope, priorities and dependencies recorded and communicated early.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Our Values</strong></h3><p><strong>We look for people who live our values every day:</strong></p><p><strong>Ease: we make things simple for our members and for each other.</strong></p><p><strong>Care: we look after our customers, our colleagues and our bikes.</strong></p><p><strong>Progress: we keep improving, learning and raising the bar.</strong></p><p><strong>Joy: we help kids fall in love with cycling, and enjoy the work we do.</strong></p><h3><strong>Why Bike Club?</strong></h3><p>You'll be joining a business with a clear purpose, a genuinely different proposition and significant opportunity to grow.</p><p>This is a rare opportunity to build the operating system for our national refurbishment and distribution site from the ground up, shaping how Bike Club gets the right bike to every family, right when they need it.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/bike-club/fractional-product-lead-3-month-contract-london-290448","tags":["Product Management"],"job_types":["Fixed-term contract","manager"],"location":"London","created_at":1793116847},{"slug":"programme-director-london-463803","company_name":"Wppproduction","title":"Programme Director","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message skipProofing&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About WPP Production&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;ms-outlook-mobile-reference-message skipProofing&quot;&gt;We are WPP Production - the unified global production company that brings together all of WPP&#39;s content producers, studios and craft experts into one connected organisation. We combine world-class human craft with next generation technology to originate, design, and deliver multi-channel content systems at scale. Built for borderless collaboration and powered by deep craft expertise, we are the production engine designed for today&#39;s always on, AI driven marketing world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About WPP&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands. We unite&amp;nbsp;cutting-edge media intelligence and data solutions, world-class creativity, next-generation production, transformative enterprise solutions and expert strategic counsel&amp;nbsp;in a single company –&amp;nbsp;powered by exceptional talent and our agentic marketing platform, WPP Open,&amp;nbsp;to help our clients navigate change, capture opportunity and deliver transformational growth. For more information, visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://urldefense.com/v3/__http://wpp.com/__;!!JboVxjCXSME!N9KGoZIn5nCC-uOWhEdE-ChrrJuf6TgkLzNNkLaW9BExJsVqZZ_hMSmGbARJ0tdBOnKYM7kEbv5L3ncUpg7-6uEPNdY$&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;6ded86b6-cde3-4e48-958d-34727f881edd&quot;&gt;WPP.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Hybrid working model&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;xmsonormal&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;We believe the best work happens when we&#39;re together, fostering creativity, collaboration, and connection. That&#39;s why we’ve adopted a hybrid approach, with teams in the office around four days a week. If you require accommodations or flexibility, please discuss this with the hiring team during the interview process.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;HEX brings together creative talent, emerging technology and industry-leading partners to turn innovation into scalable solutions for our clients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Programme Director to lead the end-to-end delivery of a complex, high-profile programme at the intersection of creative production, AI and emerging technology.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will translate strategic objectives into an integrated delivery plan, bring multiple workstreams together and ensure the programme delivers against its commitments. You’ll take ownership of programme governance, dependencies, risks and decisions, providing the clarity and control needed to navigate complexity and maintain momentum.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working across senior leadership, technology partners, clients and multidisciplinary delivery teams, you’ll connect the bigger picture with the detail of execution, ensuring everyone is aligned on what needs to happen, when and why.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead the programme&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the integrated programme plan, translating objectives into clear workstreams, milestones, deliverables and success measures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish effective governance, clear accountability and a consistent approach to programme reporting and decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain oversight of the critical path, dependencies and delivery commitments, ensuring activity across workstreams comes together to achieve the overall programme objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide a clear view of programme health, progress and emerging issues, giving leadership the information needed to make timely, informed decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive delivery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead delivery across multiple workstreams, aligning teams on priorities, milestones and interdependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate risks, resolve blockers and drive action on issues before they impact delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage changes to scope, timelines and deliverables, assessing their implications and ensuring trade-offs are agreed and understood.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenge assumptions, address competing priorities and keep teams focused on the outcomes that matter most.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold workstream leads accountable for commitments, following through on actions and intervening where delivery is at risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Align clients and stakeholders&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted relationships with senior stakeholders across WPP, technology partners and client organisations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create alignment across teams with different priorities, ensuring clear ownership, timely decisions and a shared understanding of programme objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead programme reviews and executive reporting, communicating progress, risks, decisions and required actions with clarity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the central point of coordination for programme delivery, connecting stakeholders and ensuring commitments translate into action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deliver measurable outcomes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain oversight of performance against programme objectives, milestones, budgets and agreed commercial commitments, working with the relevant commercial and finance leads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and track success measures that demonstrate client adoption, business impact and value delivered.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify emerging delivery or commercial risks, making their implications visible and driving appropriate action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use performance data and programme insight to inform decisions, address underperformance and improve outcomes throughout the programme lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience leading complex programmes involving multiple workstreams, interdependent deliverables and senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record of translating strategic objectives into executable plans and delivering against challenging commitments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong programme management expertise across integrated planning, governance, critical path management, risk, dependencies and change control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The judgement to anticipate problems, navigate ambiguity and make effective decisions when priorities or delivery conditions change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The confidence to challenge constructively, influence senior stakeholders and hold teams accountable across matrixed organisations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial awareness, including an understanding of budgets, forecasts and performance against agreed commitments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, with the ability to turn complex information into clear decisions, recommendations and executive-level reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive, collaborative approach, combining attention to detail with a clear focus on overall programme objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience in creative production, digital transformation, AI-enabled programmes or technology partnerships would be advantageous.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A clear, integrated programme plan that connects workstreams, milestones, dependencies and outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Predictable, well-controlled delivery, with risks anticipated, blockers resolved and commitments actively managed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear accountability across workstreams and strong alignment between clients, partners and delivery teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Timely, informed decision-making supported by transparent reporting and a reliable view of programme performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measurable client outcomes, with clear evidence of adoption, business impact and value delivered.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A programme that meets its objectives while adapting effectively as priorities and requirements evolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;#LI-HYBRID&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;#LI-RH1&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why work here:&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;At WPP Production, you’ll help shape the future of content production at a truly global scale. We bring together world-class talent, cutting-edge studios, and advanced technology to solve some of the most complex creative and production challenges in the industry. You’ll work in a collaborative, borderless environment where craft excellence is valued, innovation is encouraged, and AI and next-generation tools are used to amplify not replace human creativity. With access to diverse projects, global career opportunities, and the backing of WPP’s unmatched network, this is a place where you can grow your skills, make real impact, and create work that performs for every audience, across every channel, at every moment. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
