 serving more than 1M+ members, and have reached €800M+ in ARR.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prevention as the new norm. That's what we're building with our team of 1000+ people. If it speaks to you: we're hiring across France, Spain, Belgium, and Canada. And beyond.</p><h2><strong>⭐️ The User Researcher role ⭐️</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Alan, research is not a checkpoint. It's a compass. Our User Research team sits at the intersection of product, design, and engineering, making sure every decision is grounded in what our members actually need, feel, and experience.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a User Researcher at Alan, you will gather and prioritize the most important questions from across the company, and design the right research to answer them. That means running interviews, diary studies, surveys, and usability sessions throughout the full product cycle, not just at the end. You'll then turn those findings into insights that are clear, compelling, and genuinely useful to the teams who need them.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll work hand in hand with Product Managers, Designers, and Engineers, and collaborate closely with our analytics and data science teams to tell a complete story about our product. You'll also help grow research culture across Alan, sharing your craft and mentoring teammates along the way.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Alan, great research drives great product. If you love figuring out what people truly need and translating that into decisions that matter, this role is for you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>⭐️ If you have some of the following, you may be a great fit ⭐️</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You may be a great fit at Alan if you have:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>4+ years of experience</strong> as a product/user researcher in a tech environment, with strong hands-on expertise in qualitative methods: interviews, diary studies, think-aloud usability testing, and direct observation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Solid quantitative research skills</strong>: you're comfortable with survey design, sampling, crosstabs, and core statistical concepts</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Sharp critical thinking</strong>: you quickly identify what research is worth doing, scope it efficiently, and deliver insights that are focused and actionable</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A strategic mindset</strong>: you know how to partner with product stakeholders, communicate the value of research, and tie your findings to concrete business impact</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Compelling communication skills</strong>: you turn complex findings into clear narratives that resonate with any audience</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experience mentoring</strong> junior researchers or non-researchers, with the ability to give clear, actionable feedback that helps others grow</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You're close to AI</strong>. Either you've built AI products, or you follow the space closely and have a clear view on where to leverage and how LLM systems behave in production.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You care about healthcare</strong>. Alan's mission has to genuinely matter to you. For us this is essential, not a nice-to-have.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>English fluency</strong>, written and spoken</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>(As a plus)</em> Fluency in French, Spanish, or another European language</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">For this role, we hire within the <strong>D-E level range</strong>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>🌍 How we work</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Based in (or within commuting distance of) one of our hubs (Paris, Bordeaux, Marseille, Brussels, Madrid, or Barcelona)</strong>, with the ability to work onsite twice per week.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>🎯 Important note: we hire people, not roles.</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you're excited about this opportunity but don't check every box, we'd love to hear from you. Everyone, no matter how underrepresented, should feel free to apply, as it can only bring learnings or success.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you identify yourself as a woman: Did you know that research shows women often apply only when meeting 100% of requirements?</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Remember, this is just a guide, not a checklist. We'll be thrilled to receive your application!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🔖 Check out our<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://alan.com/about"> <u>About Alan</u></a> and<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://alan.com/careers"> <u>Career</u></a> pages, as well as our<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://medium.com/alan"> <u>Medium</u></a>,<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://blog.alan.com/"> <u>blog</u></a> and<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.glassdoor.com/Overview/Working-at-Alan-EI_IE1696043.11,15.htm"> <u>Glassdoor page</u></a> for more info.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You want to know more about Alan?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🙌<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://alan.com/en/careers/a/salary-equity"> <strong><u>Perks &amp; Benefits</u></strong></a>: Alaners are provided with a stimulating environment and perks ensuring they are happy, efficient and spend only high-quality time with co-workers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🤘<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://alan.com/en/about/a/leadership-principles"> <strong><u>A strong cul