d deep learning team with researchers who have pushed the state of the art in academia and industry.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Research Intern, you will be paired up with one or more members of our core software development team, assuming direct ownership of a project that meaningfully advances the capabilities of our team and products.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you have a strong foundation in math, theory, and software development and you are interested in directly contributing to the development of the next generation of autonomy algorithms and pushing them into real products, we would love to hear from you.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h3><strong>Areas of Responsibility:</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Core Simulator Architecture</strong>: Design, implement, and evolve the foundational architecture of the Skydio Simulator, ensuring it scales across vehicle types, environments, and use cases.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Physics and Dynamics</strong>: Improve and extend physics models governing vehicle motion, interactions with the environment, and dynamic agents.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Sensor and Hardware Simulation</strong>: Build high-fidelity simulations of cameras, IMUs, and other onboard components, including timing, noise characteristics, and hardware behavior.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Autonomy Stack Integration</strong>: Run and validate the full Skydio autonomy stack in simulation, ensuring consistency between simulated and real-world behavior.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Feature Development on Top of the Core</strong>: Implement simulator capabilities that unlock new workflows for customers and internal autonomy engineers, from training scenarios to advanced testing modes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Performance and Fidelity</strong>: Profile, optimize, and improve simulator performance while continuously pushing realism and accuracy.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>What You’ll Do:</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop core simulator components in C++ and Python, working close to real-time constraints.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with autonomy, perception, and controls engineers to align simulation behavior with real-world systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Debug complex interactions between physics, sensors, autonomy logic, and rendering.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help shape the long-term technical direction of the simulator as both a product and an internal platform.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to documentation and shared understanding of how the simulator works internally.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Qualifications:</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong software engineering experience with C++ and Python.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building complex systems where performance, determinism, or correctness matter.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort reasoning about time-synchronized systems, state machines, or real-time execution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to work in a large, evolving codebase with multiple stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interest in robotics, simulation, or physical systems (prior robotics experience is a plus, not a requirement).</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Bonus Experience:</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Robotics, simulation, game engines, or real-time systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Physics engines, sensor modeling, or hardware abstraction layers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Multithreaded or low-latency system design.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience debugging systems that span software and physical behavior.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Compensation:</strong> The hourly rate for this position is $47/hr for Undergrad, $53/hr for Masters, and $70/hr for PhD students*. Compensation will vary based on factors, including skill level, proficiencies, transferable knowledge, and experience. In addition to base salary, Skydio full-time employees are eligible to enroll in our benefit plans and take advantage of a variety of incentives and stipends. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">*Compensation for certain positions may vary based on the position's location.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">#LI-DK1</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Skydio we believe that diversity drives innovation. We have created a multidisciplinary environment that embraces the power of diverse perspectives to create elegant solutions for complex problems. We are committed to growing our network of people, programs, and resources to nurture an inclusive culture.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or other characteristics protected by federal, state or local anti-discrimination laws.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For positions located in the United States of America, Skydio, Inc. uses E-Verify to confirm employment eligibility. To learn more about E-Verify, including your rights and responsibilities, please visit <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.e-verify.gov/">https://www.e-verify.gov/</a></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/skydio/autonomy-engineer-intern-simulation-robotics-2027-zurich-101548","tags":["R&D"],"job_types":["Intern"],"location":"Zurich, Switzerland","created_at":1793126438},{"slug":"autonomy-engineer-intern-autonomy-infrastructure-systems-and-tools-2027-zurich-280117","company_name":"Skydio","title":"Autonomy Engineer Intern, Autonomy Infrastructure, Systems and Tools, 2027 (Zurich)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Skydio is the leading US drone company and the world leader in autonomous flight, the key technology for the future of drones and aerial mobility. The Skydio team combines deep expertise in artificial intelligence, best-in-class hardware and software product development, operational excellence, and customer obsession to empower a broader, more diverse audience of drone users, from <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.skydio.com/solutions/energy-and-utilities">utility inspectors</a> to <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.skydio.com/solutions/public-safety">first responders</a>, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.skydio.com/solutions/national-security/tactical-isr">soldiers in battlefield scenarios</a>, and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.skydio.com/solutions">beyond</a>.</p><h2><strong>About the Role:</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The core of our system is the computer vision algorithms that allow drones to understand the world around them. You will architect and implement the algorithms that run on every drone powered by Skydio as part of a world class computer vision and deep learning team with researchers who have pushed the state of the art in academia and industry.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Research Intern, you will be paired up with one or more members of our core software development team, assuming direct ownership of a project that meaningfully advances the capabilities of our team and products.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you have a strong foundation in math, theory, and software development and you are interested in directly contributing to the development of the next generation of autonomy algorithms and pushing them into real products, we would love to hear from you.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>Areas of Responsibility:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Design and build robust replay and analysis systems</strong> that enable engineers to inspect and reproduce recorded autonomy behavior, with fine-grained control over system state, perception outputs, and decision-making at every stage of the stack.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Develop scalable infrastructure for automated testing and failure triage</strong>, expanding our simulation and log-driven test coverage while accelerating root-cause analysis through automated log processing and diagnostics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Operate at the interface between autonomy software and core robotics middleware</strong>, defining clear APIs, data contracts, and performance requirements for messaging, state propagation, and coordination across subsystems, while partnering closely with downstream teams to support their implementation and integration.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Design and implement high-quality developer infrastructure and tools</strong> that prioritize reliability, performance, and usability, enabling rapid iteration, safe experimentation, and sustained velocity across the autonomy organization.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What You’ll Do:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead the design and implementation of scalable tools used across autonomy development and testing workflows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with autonomy, QA, and infrastructure teams to gather requirements, align on priorities, and deliver impactful tooling.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build tools that streamline stages of the robotics development process.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take ownership of internal services from concept through deployment and monitoring.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to the long-term vision and roadmap for developer tools that improve debugging efficiency, test coverage, and system understanding.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Qualifications:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficiency in C++ and Python, with a strong grasp of performance-sensitive and multi-threaded systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with simulation frameworks, time-synchronized data systems, or state-machine-driven applications.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with structured data visualization, log processing, or developer tooling design.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong communication skills and the ability to partner effectively with cross-functional teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort operating in a fast-paced environment where requirements evolve and priorities shift.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Bonus Experience:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building performance-sensitive systems (profiling, multithreading, real-time constraints) in robotics, aerospace, automotive, or similar domains.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exposure to robotics / simulation / physics engines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Background in telemetry systems, log ingestion pipelines, or automated test environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Front-end development skills in modern web frameworks (e.g., React, TypeScript, Three.js, Plotly) with a focus on data interaction and visualization.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with distributed systems or cloud-hosted services used to support internal tools and customer applications.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Compensation:</strong> The hourly rate for this position is $47/hr for Undergrad, $53/hr for Masters, and $70/hr for PhD students*. Compensation will vary based on factors, including skill level, proficiencies, transferable knowledge, and experience. In addition to base salary, Skydio full-time employees are eligible to enroll in our benefit plans and take advantage of a variety of incentives and stipends. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">*Compensation for certain positions may vary based on the position's location.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">#LI-DK1</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Skydio we believe that diversity drives innovation. We have created a multidisciplinary environment that embraces the power of diverse perspectives to create elegant solutions for complex problems. We are committed to growing our network of people, programs, and resources to nurture an inclusive culture.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or other characteristics protected by federal, state or local anti-discrimination laws.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For positions located in the United States of America, Skydio, Inc. uses E-Verify to confirm employment eligibility. To learn more about E-Verify, including your rights and responsibilities, please visit <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.e-verify.gov/">https://www.e-verify.gov/</a></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/skydio/autonomy-engineer-intern-autonomy-infrastructure-systems-and-tools-2027-zurich-280117","tags":["R&D"],"job_types":["Intern"],"location":"Zurich, Switzerland","created_at":1793126438},{"slug":"head-of-operations-zurich-100-117736","company_name":"Loki","title":"Head of Operations (Zürich, 100%)","description":"<h2>We are hiring a Head of Operations</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />⏰ Start date: ASAP</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">📍Zürich, Switzerland (on-site, remote not possible)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🦾 Full-time (100%)<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Loki Robotics’ mission is to make physical services an abundant commodity for everyone through robotics and physical AI. We build, deploy and operate expert robots with unique capabilities to automate commercial facility services at scale. We believe emergent capabilities in physical AI are unlocked by taking a straight shot to useful, performant robots deployed in the real world. We’re a tight team that takes initiative, operates with agency, and genuinely cares about doing outstanding work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Your role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Every robot we produce has to be prepared, shipped, deployed, operated, serviced and improved in the field. As Head of Operations, you own that end to end. You are the execution engine that customers and the rest of Loki rely on to make deployments happen, and you build the operations organization that keeps getting better at it: more automated, more productized and spread across more roles and geographies as we scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you will be doing</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own deployment implementation: site assessments, customer kick-offs, onsite supervision, staff training, performance assessment and all customer communication along the way</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run logistics for every deployment: fulfillment, shipping, import/export, compliance and coordination with the customer’s receiving side</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and run the operations organization: SOPs, scheduling, allocating operator bandwidth across deployments, testing and internal data collection, among others</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with our testing engineers on release, performance and quality assurance testing: reporting procedures, schedules and the bandwidth to execute them</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Relay what customers and field operations tell you back to product, GTM and R&amp;D</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Find operations bottlenecks and remove them, whether through a new process, a new hire, a change in structure or by killing a process entirely. Many ops tasks exist because a feature is missing or because that is how it has always been done. Your job is to delete, automate or productize them</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hire, onboard and lead the operations team: define roles, onboarding, incentives, internal assessments and the KPIs that steer our operations organization</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Train partner operators and distributors in deployment operations as we expand</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you should have</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years in operations, field deployment, implementation or a comparable role combining management and execution-heavy tasks. You have managed teams for a meaningful part of that experience</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have built an operations function at an early-stage company from the ground up, without a support structure already in place for you to consume</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have deployed physical products at customer sites: hardware, robotics, automation or industrial equipment. Robotics or facility services is a strong plus</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You operate across both horizons at once: what has to happen in the next 12 hours and what the org needs to look like in 3 months. You know at any moment what the top priority is and what to delegate</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are hands-on. An undefined process, a missing checklist or one overworked colleague is enough for you to act, fixing it for tomorrow and making sure it does not come back</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are the best manager in the room. You set clear goals, put people where their strengths accelerate the team and get along with people from all walks of life.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are detail-oriented and think from first principles, and you can turn that into clear, robust processes that others can just follow</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You take action on a goal without waiting for direction, and ask for help when you need it without letting that block you</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication in English</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What we offer</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ownership of Loki’s deployment, internal operations and field ops end-to-end</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The opportunity to build and lead the operations org as we scale across geographies</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Close partnership with the founders/leadership team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flat hierarchy, quick decision making and real responsibility in executing Loki’s global expansion</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be at the forefront of changing how physical services are delivered</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Don’t worry if you don’t hit every checkmark. We value people who learn fast and care about building great products. If Loki excites you and you believe you can help us scale, just give it a go and apply.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />At Loki, you are accepted for who you are. We welcome applicants of every background, gender, age and nationality. Different experiences and perspectives make our team and our product better.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/loki/head-of-operations-zurich-100-117736","tags":["Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Zürich","created_at":1793126438},{"slug":"account-manager-emea-zurich-36238","company_name":"Benchling","title":"Account Manager - EMEA","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are rebuilding biotech for the AI era.<br /><br />When a breakthrough is delayed, the world waits. Getting a molecule from discovery to patients, or a crop from lab to field, involves thousands of slow, manual, disconnected steps. AI has the potential to change this, compressing decades of R&amp;D work into years. But that only happens when clean, structured scientific data and AI are built into how science gets done.<br /><br />Benchling is the AI platform for biotech R&amp;D. Scientists use Benchling to design experiments, capture structured data, and run AI agents and models directly in their workflows. Over 200,000 scientists around the world trust Benchling to power their most important work, from academic labs to Sanofi, Moderna, and more than half of the world's top 50 biopharma.<br /><br />We’re building an AI scientist for our customers. We can’t do that if we haven’t built the muscle ourselves. AI fluency is the foundation we build on; it's core to how we work, and we're committed to helping every new hire integrate it into their day-to-day. As part of our interview process, you'll complete a brief AI-focused exercise or discussion so we can understand how you think about and use AI to drive impact in your role. Feel free to reference any tools, platforms, or workflows you use today.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>ROLE OVERVIEW</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Benchling believes in putting our customers at the center of everything we do. We strive to provide an exceptional experience for our customers and our users from the first touchpoint, through our implementations, and once they are live. We take pride in our world-class renewal rates, and Account Management is an essential part of this equation. To keep up with our rapidly expanding growth, we have a team of seasoned Account Managers with experience in Life Sciences, who can help grow the organization, develop our processes, and drive execution.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our Account Manager team works alongside our Professional Services, Product, Sales and technical teams to help our most strategic customers enhance the value of their Benchling investments. Account Managers will engage regularly and strategize directly with our customers to ensure long term value. Alongside the client, they will develop strategies and tactics to understand the health of the client, own renewal negotiations and execution and drive expansion of success packages. Through regular engagements with the clients, Account Managers will identify clients who can benefit from a product or technical subject matter expert related to areas of improvement, and direct them to the approapriate team to drive progress on customer initiatives.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"> </p><h2><strong>RESPONSIBILITIES</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain productive relationships with key stakeholders across Scientific and IT functional areas including customer champions and economic buyers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience managing complex customers with highly technical implementations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Utilize customer engagement models throughout the lifetime customer journey to ensure customer satisfaction, governance, expansion opportunity in order to maximize value.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use strong processes and systems are in place so that trends in customer contraction and churn are identified early, communicated with the appropriate audience, and appropriate follow-up action is taken</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage the renewal experience,identify and define client challenges or new scientific business case opportunities aligned with the customers’ objectives and vision with support from the extended Benchling team to client success and avoid contraction/churn.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience negotiating upwards of $100,000 in ARR for renewals and expansions in collaboration with sales to drive accurate forecasting around adoption, expansion and retention.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"> </p><h2><strong>QUALIFICATIONS</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">BS or M.Sc. in Biology, Molecular Biology, Genetics, Biotechnology, Bioengineering or experience working in the Life Sciences field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2+ years of Account management, Customer Success, Renewal Management, Sales, Professional Services, or Consulting experience in a SaaS software environment with the ability to forge relationships with users, decision makers, and influential stakeholders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2+ years commercial experience in negotiations utilizing skills to handle contract discussions and ensure favorable outcomes for both the customer and the company</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An understanding of Life Sciences R&amp;D processes and scientific concepts is preferred. Demonstrated ability to immediately interface and build trust with Scientists, as well as Director &amp; VP Level Business and IT leaders in top Biotech and Pharma companies</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication skills, able to communicate confidently and concisely in verbal, written and presentation formats to all types of audiences</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Self-motivated, independent, adaptable, and can thrive in a fast-paced startup environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to travel 10-20% based on customer needs</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"> </p><h2>HOW WE WORK</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We offer a flexible hybrid work arrangement that prioritizes in-office collaboration. Employees are expected to be on-site 3 days per week (Monday, Tuesday, and Thursday).<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">#LI-Hybrid </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">#BI-Hybrid </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benchling welcomes everyone.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe diversity enriches our team so we hire people with a wide range of identities, backgrounds, and experiences. <br /><br />We are an equal opportunity employer. That means we don’t discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, or disability status. We also consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable federal, state and local law, including but not limited to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/benchling/account-manager-emea-zurich-36238","tags":["Customer Experience"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Zurich, Switzerland","created_at":1793126437},{"slug":"senior-fullstack-engineer-zurich-83613","company_name":"BLP Digital AG","title":"Senior Fullstack Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Join BLP and help make the world’s business processes autonomous! </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our agentic platform helps finance and operations teams worldwide remove manual work from their core business processes, so work runs end-to-end with greater control and significant productivity gains. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today, over 550 enterprise customers use BLP across 1,300+ deployed projects. In the processes we automate, customers achieve productivity improvements of 5 to 10 times. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To date, BLP remains majority employee-owned, with Goldman Sachs holding a minority stake as a growth investor. Our success is driven by deep expertise in technology and business processes, a superior product with strong product-market fit, reflected in an expanding customer base that includes Fortune 500 companies. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">BLP is one of Switzerland's fastest-growing SaaS scale-ups; we are now entering our next phase of growth. From our headquarters on Zürich's Bahnhofstrasse, we're expanding globally, with a growing presence across Europe and North America. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Join us and help make autonomous operations the new standard. </em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>The team</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">At blp, dedicated engineering teams own individual products such as invoices, customer orders, and order confirmations. The Platform Team owns what all of them are built on: shared services and APIs, the data access layer, and the component and design system that shape how the product looks and behaves.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The team's focus has been the frontend platform, and we are now deliberately extending that ownership deeper into the stack. You would be central to that shift, with real influence over how the platform layer gets defined rather than inheriting someone else's blueprint.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2>About the role</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do and for whom.</strong> You build and run the core backend service our product teams rely on, from its APIs and persistence layer to email, user provisioning, and cross-tenant capabilities for large enterprises. Through those teams, your work reaches the 20'000+ people who use our Purchase-to-Pay and Order-to-Cash agents every day.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Where you'll work.</strong> You join the Platform Team, about 10 engineers. At BLP, platform means the core of our product, not internal infrastructure: the shared services, data access layer, and design system that every product runs on. You work closely with the senior backend engineer who owns these areas today, in a large production Go codebase with well-established patterns.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What success looks like.</strong> In your first year, you own one core area end-to-end, for example, user provisioning, outbound email, cross-tenant capabilities, analytics, or workflow configuration, from the Go service to the customer using it.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2>What you'll do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build the service that product teams build on.</strong> Design, build, and evolve the core APIs behind document processing, approval workflows, administration, and analytics, with clear contracts so product teams can ship on top of them without workarounds.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own the persistence layer.</strong> Each tenant has its own isolated MySQL database. You evolve the abstraction product teams build on (a tenant-scoped unit of work, typed repositories, and shared type-safe querying) so that isolation, transactions, and permissions are right by default.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Scale BLP for large enterprises.</strong> Extend our cross-tenant capabilities so customers with many subsidiaries and business units can manage users, permissions, and documents across all of them from one place, correctly, securely, and fast.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own email, in and out.</strong> Own our email document ingestion and outbound email services, including the audit trail and its UI.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Make setup self-service.</strong> Turn manual SSO, SCIM, and email setups into migration tools and admin UIs that customers and project managers can run on their own.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work with customers.</strong> Join onboarding calls with customer IT teams and project managers, get their setups running, and turn what you learn into better tooling.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own it end-to-end.</strong> From the Go service through the React UI to production, including tracing, metrics, and incident analysis after it ships.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Tech stack:</strong> Go, React/TypeScript, MySQL, Redis, Temporal, Kubernetes on GCP and AWS, GitHub CI/CD, and OpenTelemetry with Grafana, Prometheus, Tempo, and Parca for observability.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>We're excited about you because</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have <strong>4+ years of experience as a software engineer</strong>, with most of that time spent building and operating backend systems in production.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have <strong>2+ years of professional Go experience</strong>, writing services that run in production, not side projects.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've designed a backend service or API that other teams depended on, and kept it reliable and evolvable as usage grew.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You work well across teams. You align with product, integration, and infrastructure teams on contracts, priorities, and rollouts, and you can explain technical trade-offs to people who aren't engineers.</p></li><l