efore hardware/firmware generation changes.</p></li><li><p><strong>Optimize the Portfolio:</strong> Maintain a structured view of all variants (terminal types, SoftPOS vs. hardware POS) using frameworks like the BCG matrix to prioritize investment and avoid overlap/cannibalization.</p></li><li><p><strong>Build Capacity-Synced Roadmaps:</strong> Translate strategic goals and vertical needs into prioritized, time-boxed feature roadmaps (e.g., quarterly or PI planning in SAFe), balancing "run the business" compliance updates against "grow the business" initiatives.</p></li><li><p><strong>Champion Vertical Expertise & Research:</strong> Act as the "translator" between vertical requirements (e.g., retail, hospitality, events) and engineering's technical language while running ongoing trend scanning (PCI/EMV updates), competitor analysis, and customer feedback synthesis.</p></li><li><p><strong>Lead Go-to-Market & Sales Enablement:</strong> Define launch plans (positioning, pricing, training, documentation), coordinate alignment across Sales, Marketing, and Support, and assist Sales with technical expertise on complex, regulated deals.</p></li><li><p><strong>Manage Suppliers & Ecosystems:</strong> Onboard and manage external partners (terminal manufacturers, component suppliers, certification labs), overseeing SLAs, operational forecasting, defect escalations, contract negotiations, and risk mitigation (such as dual-sourcing).</p></li></ul><h3><strong>What Success Looks Like</strong></h3><ul><li><p><strong>Strategic Portfolio Health:</strong> A clear, non-overlapping product line where investments are prioritized effectively and End-of-Sale (EOS) / End-of-Life (EOL) migration paths are seamlessly executed.</p></li><li><p><strong>Uncompromising Compliance:</strong> Continuous alignment with certification and regulatory standards (PCI, EMV, ep2) across the entire portfolio, eliminating compliance risk.</p></li><li><p><strong>Reliable Supplier Alignment:</strong> High-performing partner relationships with well-managed SLAs, aligned roadmaps, and secure supply chains.</p></li><li><p><strong>Market-Driven Innovation:</strong> Roadmaps and GTM materials that accurately reflect vertical user journeys, market trends, and validated customer needs.</p></li><li><p><strong>Cross-Functional Readiness:</strong> Seamless coordination with internal teams so all departments are aligned and fully enabled from day one of product launches.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>What You Bring to the Table</strong></h3><ul><li><p><strong>Product Experience:</strong> Proven experience in product management, ideally with portfolio or product line ownership in fintech, payments, or hardware-enabled software.</p></li><li><p><strong>Domain Knowledge:</strong> Understanding or familiarity with payment certification and compliance topics (PCI, EMV, ep2) is a strong plus.</p></li><li><p><strong>Vertical & Market Expertise:</strong> Experience or strong interest in specific industry verticals, coupled with a track record in market research and competitor analysis.</p></li><li><p><strong>Strategic & Analytical Mindset:</strong> Strong problem-solving skills with a solution- and customer-oriented approach.</p></li><li><p><strong>Stakeholder & Supplier Management:</strong> Exceptional communication and negotiation skills, comfortable managing both internal stakeholders and external supplier relationships.</p></li><li><p><strong>Languages:</strong> Fluent in English and German.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Why Join Wallee?</strong></h3><ul><li><p><strong>Modern Workspace:</strong> A beautiful office in the heart of <strong>Winterthur</strong> - comfortable, bright, and collaboration-ready.</p></li><li><p><strong>True Flexibility:</strong> Flexible daily hours and a <strong>4-week "Work from Anywhere"</strong> policy every year.</p></li><li><p><strong>Innovation First:</strong> We work with the latest tech stacks in a flat hierarchy where your voice actually matters.</p></li><li><p><st