search & Development"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Delft","created_at":1793126439},{"slug":"interim-qa-specialist-utrecht-458492","company_name":"Rentman","title":"Interim QA Specialist","description":"<h1><strong>About us</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rentman is a B2B SaaS scale-up building a smart, powerful operations management platform to support event and media production teams. Our users plan everything from small shoots to massive festivals in 70+ countries, and they all rely on Rentman to keep their gear, people, and timing perfectly in sync. We’re based in Utrecht (NL) with a second office in Toronto (CA), and our 100+ team members work in a culture that’s open, flat, and inclusive, where curiosity drives us, ownership matters, and everyone has the freedom to challenge ideas and make an impact. Check out our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://rentman.io/public-roadmap">public roadmap</a> to see what’s coming next!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><div style="text-align:left"><img style="max-width:100%" src="https://app.ashbyhq.com/api/images/user-content/d722c125-c3d1-4d3f-8dbf-08d8ac4ab137/1abd1b97-44fa-4e7c-92e0-d04d95cf059f/Screenshot_2026-07-22_at_17.03.37.png" /></div><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Mission of this role</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">As an interim Senior QA Specialist at Rentman, you make sure every release reaches customers without regressions. You own the test strategy across our 3 product teams and finish moving regression testing from a manual release-day cycle to an automated, shift-left E2E suite. Without this role, quality depends on manual testing on release day, bugs show up in staging or production, and the move to automated testing stalls. This is an interim position: the duration is still to be confirmed, and the role ends once the assignment is complete.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What you'll do</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join refinement with the product teams and write Gherkin (Given/When/Then) acceptance specs that developers turn into tests</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Test new features on staging, going beyond the acceptance criteria to find edge cases, and file clear, reproducible bug reports in Jira</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write and review Playwright tests (TypeScript) in the frontend repo, and review developer-written tests in pull requests</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor the daily automated regression run in GitHub Actions, triage failures the same day, and fix flaky tests at the root cause</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run release-day regression and the OWASP ZAP security scan for each release, and give a clear go / no-go call</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Migrate the remaining legacy tests and decide what is worth automating and what stays manual</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Organise cross-team QA days and coach developers so they own their tests</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div></li></ul><div style="text-align:left"><img style="max-width:100%" src="https://app.ashbyhq.com/api/images/user-content/d722c125-c3d1-4d3f-8dbf-08d8ac4ab137/3c95dc18-9519-4446-b1af-13a805537681/Screenshot_2026-07-23_at_10.38.46.png" /></div><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What we are looking for </strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years in QA on web applications</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At least 2 years writing and maintaining UI test automation in code (Playwright, Cypress or Selenium, ideally TypeScript/JavaScript), not only record-and-play tools</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong manual and exploratory testing, with bug reports developers can act on without follow-up questions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have defined a test strategy (what to automate, what to test manually, coverage), not only executed test cases</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience running automated tests in CI (GitHub Actions or similar)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You get developers to adopt new habits through pairing, good examples and clear specs, not by policing</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div></li></ul><h2><strong>Nice to haves</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with complex B2B SaaS</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Playwright specifically, and Gherkin / BDD</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience leading a shift-left change or coaching developers to own their tests</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">API testing (REST, Postman or similar)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Basic security testing (e.g. OWASP ZAP)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mobile app testing (iOS / Android)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What you’ll get </strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive salary based on experience, plus 8% holiday allowance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A results-based bonus based on company performance (up to a full 13th month's salary)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">25 vacation days to recharge</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Earn an extra day of PTO for each year at Rentman, from your second anniversary up to five years.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A 4-week paid sabbatical after 5 years to go on an adventure</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible WFH policy &amp; work from anywhere for 4 weeks a year</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pension plan through BrightPensioen</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An annual training budget to grow your skills</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Access to OpenUp for mental well-being and personal growth</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your choice of a shiny new Windows, Linux, or Mac</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stay active with the team: join the Rentman football team, squash and padel, plus a discounted Urban Sports membership</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An OV Business card if you live more than 10km from the office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An ambitious, inclusive, and diverse international team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A flexible, energizing workplace with free lunches, office perks (PS5, ping pong, D&amp;D), legendary karaoke nights, and regular team activities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An amazing office in the heart of Utrecht, in the historic Drift 17</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Our process</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Here's a breakdown of our recruitment process to give you a clear idea:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Introduction Call with the recruiter about the job &amp; Rentman, online (30 mins)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Past Experience &amp; Culture Interview with the team, online or on-site (60 mins)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Final Skills Interview, on-site (60 mins)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />Apply now! For questions or additional information, contact us at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" ---------- style="min-height:1.5em"><em><br />At Rentman, we value diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. We believe that our differences make us stronger and strive to foster a workplace where everyone feels valued and respected.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/rentman/interim-qa-specialist-utrecht-458492","tags":["R&D"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Utrecht","created_at":1793126439},{"slug":"senior-manager-product-and-gtm-enablement-amsterdam-52699","company_name":"Datasnipper","title":"Senior Manager - Product and GTM Enablement","description":"<h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a Senior Manager - Product &amp; GTM Enablement to lead and grow our Revenue Enablement function. You will own our enablement strategy and lead a team of two, ensuring the entire Revenue organization is equipped to sell, implement, and support DataSnipper with confidence.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will be the connective tissue between Product, Product Marketing, and our Revenue organization, ensuring that every new product release, capability update, and strategic shift is understood, internalized, and actionable by our field teams. You will work closely with PMs and the broader Product team to translate roadmap developments into role-specific enablement that reaches leaders, managers, and individual contributors alike.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role requires someone who can operate autonomously, manage and develop a small team, and move quickly in a fast-paced environment without sacrificing quality or alignment.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>About DataSnipper</strong></h2><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe trust is essential to how society works. Every day, we rely on information that's been independently verified, from financial statements to the products we buy, to the sustainability claims companies make. Behind that trust are audit and finance professionals who examine evidence, verify information and hold organizations accountable.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At DataSnipper, we build AI solutions that empower those professionals to make those judgements. With Alwin by DataSnipper, our new agentic platform, AI agents now take on end-to-end audit and finance procedures, while every conclusion stays traceable to its source. That frees professionals to focus on the judgment and expertise that make their work so important.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're trusted by Fortune 500 companies, government agencies and all Big Four audit firms. Today, more than <strong>600,000 professionals across 3,000+ organizations in 175 countries </strong>rely on our platform, and in 2025 alone DataSnipper delivered more than <strong>$1.4 billion</strong> in productivity savings to its customers.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Backed by a $100 million Series B led by Index Ventures, at a $1 billion valuation, we've built a strong foundation for what's next. And as proud members of 1% for the Planet, we care about how we grow, not just how fast.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What You Will Do</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>Team Leadership and Management</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead, manage, and develop a team of two Enablement Managers, setting clear goals, providing regular coaching, and creating space for them to grow</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the team's roadmap and prioritization, ensuring work is aligned to the highest-leverage opportunities across the Revenue organization</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Operate autonomously with strong judgment on when to escalate versus drive independently</p></li></ul><h3>Product Enablement and GTM Readiness</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner closely with Product Managers and Product Marketing to stay ahead of the roadmap, translating upcoming releases into role-specific enablement before they reach the field</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and deliver launch enablement for new product features and capabilities, ensuring leaders, managers, and ICs are equipped to speak to and demonstrate them confidently</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain a scalable product knowledge infrastructure including training materials, release notes for the field, and quick-reference guides that keeps the team current as the product evolves</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Serve as the go-to internal resource for questions about how DataSnipper works, what has changed, and how to position new capabilities</p></li></ul><h3>Revenue Enablement Programs</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and deliver enablement programs that span the full revenue team including AEs, CSMs, SEs, and frontline managers, aligned to where they are in the customer lifecycle</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and run discovery, value realization, and objection-handling training that prepares the field for tough conversations with technical and finance buyers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and maintain playbooks, training workbooks, and enablement assets that provide consistent depth and are usable by a global team across time zones</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Measure the impact of enablement programs through clear metrics and use data to continuously improve quality, coverage, and field performance</p></li></ul><h3>Cross-functional Collaboration</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as the primary point of contact between Product, PMM, and the Revenue org for all enablement-related alignment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build strong relationships with Revenue leaders and managers to surface gaps, gather feedback, and ensure enablement stays relevant</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to a culture of continuous learning across the Revenue organization</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What You Bring</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">7+ years of experience in revenue enablement, sales enablement, or a closely adjacent role within B2B SaaS</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated experience managing or leading a team, with the ability to set direction, give feedback, and develop people</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven ability to work closely with Product and PMM to translate roadmap developments into field-ready enablement at pace</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience building enablement programs from scratch including training curricula, playbooks, and launch frameworks, not just delivering pre-made content</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong communication and facilitation skills with the ability to simplify complex concepts and hold a room across levels of seniority</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable operating autonomously and making prioritization calls without needing heavy direction</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Data-driven approach to identifying gaps and measuring the impact of enablement on field performance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working across global, distributed teams and comfortable working across time zones</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to manage up, across, and down, influencing without authority and keeping key stakeholders aligned</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in audit, finance, or accounting technology is a strong plus</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What We Offer:</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be part of one of the fastest-growing, profitable unicorn scale-ups in the Netherlands with a global impact</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Equity (Stock Appreciation Rights) to share the company's success and growth