cal conversations with technical and finance audiences</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Continuously analyze and improve field performance through data-driven insights, tracking the connection between enablement and adoption, delivery quality, and customer outcomes</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you bring</strong><br /></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3-5 years of experience in technical enablement, solutions engineering, sales engineering, or a similar technical-plus-customer-facing role within B2B SaaS</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Direct experience translating complex or technical product concepts into clear, practical guidance that non-technical audiences can use immediately</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience building technical training programs, workshops, or enablement content from scratch (not just delivering pre-made content)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of how enterprise software products work at an architectural level. You don't need to write code, but you need to understand how the pieces fit together</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to work across teams (Product, PMM, SE, CS) and synthesize input from multiple sources into coherent enablement materials</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working with data to identify performance gaps and measure the impact of enablement programs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication and facilitation skills. You can hold a room (virtual or in-person) and make technical concepts accessible</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A collaborative, self-starter mindset suited for a fast-paced scale-up environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in audit, finance, or accounting technology is a strong plus but not required</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What We Offer:</strong><br /></h2><ul s